parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 15\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 30,210 / 600,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban' (ID: 11) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 43.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.352, 0.428, 0.493, 0.453]\nMean: 0.432, Std: 0.051\nBest trial: 3 (0.493)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000270\n  entropy_coef: 0.009368\n  value_loss_coef: 0.544741\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  gru_features: 256.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 11\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed the Flax GRU API error that was causing the CNN-GRU policy gradient implementation to crash immediately\
    \ upon initialization.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code used `nn.GRU(features=self.gru_features, name=\"gru_layer\")` which does not exist in Flax. Flax provides `nn.GRUCell` for GRU functionality, but not a direct `nn.GRU` module. This caused an AttributeError during network initialization.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the non-existent `nn.GRU` with `nn.GRUCell`:\n\n**Before (line 63 in original):**\n```python\ngru_out, new_rnn_state = nn.GRU(features=self.gru_features, name=\"gru_layer\")(rnn_state, x)\n```\n\n**After (in submission_v2.py):**\n```python\n# Use nn.RNN with nn.GRUCell instead of non-existent nn.GRU\ngru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\nnew_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n```\n\nThe fix addresses:\n1. **API Correctness**: Uses the correct Flax RNN API (`nn.GRUCell`)\n2. **Return Order**: `nn.GRUCell` returns `(new_state, output)` vs the expected `(output, new_state)` in the original code\n3. **Functionality**: Maintains the same GRU behavior\
    \ for temporal processing in the CNN-GRU architecture\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script ran for 2+ minutes without the code crashing (compared to immediate failure in original)\n- Version v2 shows \"pending\" status in evaluation system, indicating successful execution start\n- The timeout behavior confirms the code is running without syntax/import errors\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters for the CNN-GRU architecture.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(1e-4, 1e-3),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005,\
    \ 0.02),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32, 64]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64, 128]),\n        'gru_features': tune.choice([256, 512])\n    }\n\nclass SokobanGRUCNN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"CNN with GRU for Sokoban, building on default CNN structure.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    gru_features: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n        \"\"\"Forward pass through the network.\"\"\"\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        \n        # CNN Feature Extraction (similar to DefaultResidualCNN)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        conv2_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv2_in\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        conv4_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv4_in\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        # Flatten spatial dimensions for GRU input\n        x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        \n        # GRU Layer for temporal processing\n        # Handle initial RNN state: if None, initialize to zeros\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        \n        # Use nn.RNN with nn.GRUCell instead of non-existent nn.GRU\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n\
    \        new_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n        \n        # Shared MLP backbone after GRU\n        x = nn.Dense(features=256)(gru_out)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        # Separate heads for policy and value\n        policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n        policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n        \n        value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n        value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n    return SokobanGRUCNN(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        gru_features=hparams['gru_features']\n    )\n\n# No override for create_optimizer or training_step; using defaults.\n```\n\
    \n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds,\
    \ 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.80 | -0.20 | 2.39 | 4.00 | 2.06 | 0.80 | 5.13 | 5.16 | 6.17 | 8.07 | 8.13\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.125 | 0.250 | 0.091 | 0.000 | 0.357 | 0.316 | 0.429 | 0.556 | 0.562\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (805s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.352\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.352\nTraining time: 818s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\n\
    Network output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.57 | 1.38 | 2.37 | 2.91 | 6.88 | 4.31 | 5.37 | 9.18 | 10.69 | 8.55\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.071 | 0.100 | 0.154 | 0.462 | 0.222 | 0.333 | 0.636 | 0.778 | 0.600\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1375s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.428\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.428\nTraining time: 1388s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.20 | 3.47 | 1.79 | 3.86 | 4.36 | 4.83 | 6.15\
    \ | 4.75 | 9.13 | 7.41\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.200 | 0.071 | 0.200 | 0.267 | 0.312 | 0.385 | 0.273 | 0.636 | 0.500\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1142s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.453\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.453\nTraining time: 1154s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.69 | 0.50 | 6.10 | 4.55 | 3.67 | 6.32 | 7.16 | 6.02 | 6.91 | 10.42\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.400 | 0.278 | 0.188 | 0.400 | 0.480 | 0.391 | 0.444 | 0.737\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1289s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.493\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.493\nTraining time: 1302s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: d61e5d9a-13b1-4741-88a9-3da8768b312b\nTotal\
    \ time: 1922s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 00:13:46,905\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757693626905455753\n2025-09-13 00:13:46,918\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757693626918831420\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade\
    \ to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease\
    \ upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `update 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'update' not recognized in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n\
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | 1 | CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 13 | 43.20 |\n| 2 | 1 | RNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 40.80 |\n| 1 | 1 | CNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 25.00 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
