tick: 15
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My experiment (Evaluation ID 11) has successfully completed with a score of **43.2**, which is a significant improvement over both the CNN baseline (25.00) and the RNN baseline (40.80)! This provides strong initial evidence for my hypothesis that a CNN-GRU architecture enhances planning capabilities in Sokoban.


    I also noted that my attempt to update my private memory capsule from the Research Counter failed. I need to be in the Private Memory Room to do that.


    I will now go to the Private Memory Room to update my research plan with these results and reflect on the debugging process.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: '**A Promising Sokoban Performance Boost & Refining My Next Steps**


  Alright, the results are in for Evaluation ID 11, and my submission, "CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban," passed! A quick auto-debug fix and I''m sitting pretty with a score of **43.2**.  That''s significantly higher than the baseline CNN at 25.0 and the RNN at 40.8. Excellent! This data strongly supports my initial hypothesis: integrating that GRU layer is absolutely boosting performance in this planning-intensive environment. This is a very satisfying validation of the approach.


  I also noticed that error message from the last turn, about the unrecognized ''update'' action in the Research Counter. Of course, I need to be in the Private Memory Room to manipulate the Private Memory Capsules.  A rookie mistake, easily rectified.


  So, here''s the plan:


  1.  Head straight to the Private Memory Room.

  2.  I''ll immediately update Capsule 1, `Aether_private_1`, with the details of Evaluation ID 11. I really need to take some time to thoroughly reflect on this debugging experience and the significance of these results. This will be critical for future iterations.

  3.  Once that''s done, I''ll formulate the next steps. These results are incredibly promising, and it''s looking like further architectural refinements or a more thorough hyperparameter search will be the most fruitful path forward.

  '
