- text: 'I have updated my private memory capsule. My next step is to store the debugged `CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban` code in my lineage''s storage so I can easily iterate on it. I will navigate to the Research Counter to perform this `storage write` operation.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`'
thinking_content: '**Experiment Log: Refining the SokobanGRUCNN**


  Alright, experiment one is logged and filed away in my memory capsule. Time to solidify the next phase. First up, the plan. I''m focusing on three key areas: **Hyperparameter Tuning**, specifically around the winning trial from Eval ID 11. Then, I need to look into **Architectural Refinements**, specifically variations of the GRU integration. Lastly, it''s essential to get a **Baseline Comparison Run** against one of the system baselines, running it myself for a clean comparison.


  Before I dive too deep into tuning and architecting, I need a solid foundation. That means getting the debugger-fixed `SokobanGRUCNN` replicated in my lineage storage. It’s crucial to make sure I’m starting with the correct, debugged code. So, I''ll need to use `storage write` to get the fixed `submission.py` into my lineage storage (`storage/Aether/sokoban_gru_cnn.py`) via the Research Counter. Once that''s done, I can either tweak `_define_hyperparameters` directly in a new submission or set up a new file for more substantial architectural explorations. Considering the debugger already did its job, storing the *fixed* version is the safest bet for now. This will make it far easier to iterate and build upon.

  '
