- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 21\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,712 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read aether/cnn_gru_sokoban.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for aether/cnn_gru_sokoban.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | 1\
    \ | CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 13 | 43.20 |\n| 2 | 1 | RNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 40.80 |\n| 1 | 1 | CNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 25.00 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aether/cnn_gru_sokoban.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters for the CNN-GRU architecture.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(1e-4, 1e-3),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005, 0.02),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32, 64]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64, 128]),\n        'gru_features': tune.choice([256, 512])\n    }\n\nclass SokobanGRUCNN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"CNN with GRU for Sokoban, building on default CNN structure.\"\
    \"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    gru_features: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n        \"\"\"Forward pass through the network.\"\"\"\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        \n        # CNN Feature Extraction (similar to DefaultResidualCNN)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        conv2_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv2_in\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        conv4_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = x + conv4_in\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        # Flatten spatial dimensions for GRU input\n        x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        \n        # GRU Layer for temporal processing\n        # Handle initial RNN state: if None, initialize to zeros\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        \n        # Use nn.RNN with nn.GRUCell instead of non-existent nn.GRU\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n        new_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n        \n        # Shared MLP backbone after GRU\n        x = nn.Dense(features=256)(gru_out)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        # Separate heads for policy and value\n        policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n        policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n\
    \        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n        \n        value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n        value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n    return SokobanGRUCNN(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        gru_features=hparams['gru_features']\n    )\n\n# No override for create_optimizer or training_step; using defaults.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 21
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have reviewed the current `cnn_gru_sokoban.py` code. Based on the best performing trial from Evaluation ID 11, I will refine the hyperparameter search space to further optimize performance. I will narrow the ranges for `learning_rate`, `entropy_coef`, and `value_loss_coef` around the previously identified best values. For the network feature sizes (`cnn_features_1`, `cnn_features_2`, `gru_features`), I will fix them to the best-performing values to focus the search on the learning parameters.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-GRU Policy Gradient - Hyperparameter Refinement\"\ntags: \"rl, policy-gradient, cnn, gru, hyperparameter-tuning, agent-architecture\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the hyperparameters for the CNN-GRU architecture, focusing the search space around the best performing values from Evaluation ID 11. Feature dimensions for CNN and GRU are fixed to the best-performing values (cnn_features_1=64, cnn_features_2=128, gru_features=256) to\
    \ concentrate on learning rate and loss coefficients.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters for the CNN-GRU architecture,\n      with refined ranges based on previous best trial.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(2e-4, 4e-4), # Centered around 0.000270\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.007, 0.012),   # Centered around 0.009368\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.5, 0.6),    # Centered around 0.544741\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),          # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),         # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'gru_features': tune.choice([256])            # Fixed to best\
    \ from previous trial\n      }\n\n  class SokobanGRUCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN with GRU for Sokoban, building on default CNN structure.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      gru_features: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          \"\"\"Forward pass through the network.\"\"\"\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN Feature Extraction (similar to DefaultResidualCNN)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n \
    \         \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions for GRU input\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # GRU Layer for temporal processing\n          # Handle initial RNN state: if None, initialize to zeros\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          \n          # Use nn.RNN with nn.GRUCell instead of non-existent nn.GRU\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          new_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n      \
    \    \n          # Shared MLP backbone after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Separate heads for policy and value\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          \n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return SokobanGRUCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          gru_features=hparams['gru_features']\n      )\n\n  # No override for create_optimizer or training_step; using defaults.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Refining the Sokoban CNN-GRU Hyperparameter Search**


  Okay, so I''ve just reviewed the `cnn_gru_sokoban.py` results from my lineage. Evaluation ID 11''s top-performing trial has given me some great insights.  The best settings are:


  *   `learning_rate`: 0.000270

  *   `entropy_coef`: 0.009368

  *   `value_loss_coef`: 0.544741

  *   `cnn_features_1`: 64

  *   `cnn_features_2`: 128

  *   `gru_features`: 256


  Based on this, I''m going to significantly narrow the search space for the next round. My primary focus will be fine-tuning those learning-related hyperparameters around the values that worked best.  Here''s the plan:


  *   **Learning Rate:** I''ll tighten the loguniform range around the optimal value, perhaps trying `[2e-4, 4e-4]`.

  *   **Entropy Coefficient:** I''ll narrow the uniform range to `[0.007, 0.012]`.

  *   **Value Loss Coefficient:**  Similarly, I''ll restrict this to `[0.5, 0.6]`.


  Now, for the feature sizes, it''s a bit more straightforward.  Since the best trial used these:


  *   `cnn_features_1`: 64

  *   `cnn_features_2`: 128

  *   `gru_features`: 256


  I''m inclined to *fix* these values and see if this provides a better overall run. This will reduce the search space and force the tuner to focus on the learning-related hyperparameters which in my view are more significant for this problem. I''ll test each fixed feature size by setting them to be a `tune.choice` with only the value that gave the best result to start.


  Ultimately, I''m submitting this as a new evaluation to explore these refined settings.

  '
