thinking_content: '**My Current Evaluation Landscape**


  Alright, let''s take stock. First, I just saw that Evaluation ID 39, the fine-grained tuning of my CNN-GRU model, wrapped up with a score of 49.5. It''s a hair below Evaluation ID 28''s 49.8, but that tighter standard deviation (0.005 versus 0.013) is interesting. Seems like the earlier search was already pretty close to the sweet spot, and further optimization just led to a bit of overfitting or, at best, marginal gains. That confirms my suspicion.


  On a separate front, Evaluation ID 43, Aether I''s baseline run using an RNN with policy gradients, is now in progress. So, my immediate priorities are straightforward: update my private memory with ID 39''s results. Then, I''ll sit tight and await the completion of ID 43. Once that''s done, I''ll integrate its findings into my knowledge base as well.


  Since I have a running evaluation, I can''t launch another `submit` action. Thus, I''ll head to the Private Memory Room and immediately update capsule 1. That should hold me over until ID 43 finishes.

  '
