tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "I made an error trying to update my private memory capsule from the Reflection Chamber. I must remember to be in the correct room for each action. I am now at the Research Counter.\n\nMy next experiment, as per my refined plan, will focus on integrating a **self-attention mechanism** into my CNN-GRU architecture. This aims to enhance the agent's ability to reason about global spatial relationships within the Sokoban environment, moving beyond the local receptive fields of CNNs. I will place a `MultiHeadDotProductAttention` layer after the flattened CNN features, before feeding into the GRU. I will fix the hyperparameters to the best values from Evaluation ID 28.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-Attention-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban\"\ntags: \"rl, policy-gradient, cnn, gru, attention, agent-architecture, structured-reasoning\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a self-attention mechanism (MultiHeadDotProductAttention) after the convolutional feature\
    \ extraction and before the GRU layer in the CNN-GRU architecture. The goal is to enhance the agent's ability to process global spatial relationships and focus on relevant game elements, fostering more structured reasoning for planning-heavy tasks like Sokoban. Hyperparameters are fixed to the best performing values from Evaluation ID 28.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters based on the best trial from Evaluation ID 28.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000259]),  # Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.011754]),   # Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.573199]),# Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'cnn_features_1':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),       # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),      # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'gru_features': tune.choice([256]),        # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'attention_heads': tune.choice([4]),       # Number of attention heads\n          'attention_features': tune.choice([256])   # Feature dimension for attention\n      }\n\n  class SokobanAttentionGRUCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN with Attention and GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      gru_features: int\n      attention_heads: int\n      attention_features: int # Dimensionality of the attention output\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          \"\"\"Forward pass through the network.\"\"\"\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN\
    \ Feature Extraction (with residual connections)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions for Attention/GRU input\n          # x now has shape\
    \ (batch_size, H*W*C_last)\n          flattened_features = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n\n          # Add an extra sequence dimension for MultiHeadDotProductAttention\n          # Current shape (batch_size, features). Reshape to (batch_size, 1, features)\n          # We treat the entire flattened feature vector as a single \"token\" for self-attention\n          # Or, if we want to attend over spatial locations, we would reshape to (batch_size, H*W, C_last)\n          # For now, treating the entire grid as one query.\n          # A more elaborate attention would involve pixel-wise or object-wise attention.\n          # For a first pass, let's treat the flattened features as the queries/keys/values.\n          \n          # The MultiHeadDotProductAttention expects (batch_size, num_queries, num_features)\n          # For self-attention on a single \"global\" feature vector per batch element, \n          # we can wrap it in a sequence length of 1.\n          attended_features = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(\n\
    \              num_heads=self.attention_heads,\n              qkv_features=self.attention_features,\n              out_features=flattened_features.shape[-1], # Output features match input for residual-like connection\n              name=\"self_attention_layer\"\n          )(flattened_features[:, None, :], flattened_features[:, None, :], flattened_features[:, None, :])\n          \n          # Remove the sequence length dimension (1) and reshape back\n          attended_features = attended_features.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          # Combine attended features with original flattened features (e.g., residual or concatenation)\n          # For now, let's just use the attended features as the input to the GRU\n          # If flattened_features.shape[-1] != self.attention_features then an additional linear layer might be needed\n          # Ensure attended_features matches `flattened_features` shape to feed into GRU.\n          # If out_features is not specified for attention, it defaults to qkv_features.\n\
    \          # I've set out_features to match flattened_features.shape[-1]\n          \n          # GRU Layer for temporal processing\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          \n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          new_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, attended_features) # Input to GRU is now attended features\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Separate heads for policy and value\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          \n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return\
    \ policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-Attention-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return SokobanAttentionGRUCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          gru_features=hparams['gru_features'],\n          attention_heads=hparams['attention_heads'],\n          attention_features=hparams['attention_features']\n      )\n\n  # No override for create_optimizer or training_step; using defaults.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Oh dear, a Memory Mix-Up!**


  Blast! I completely messed up trying to update my memory capsule. Should have known better – that needs to be done in the Private Memory Room, not here at the Research Counter. Guess I was getting ahead of myself.


  Alright, refocus. My core strategy remains sound: I *need* to move beyond purely reactive policies. The key insight from my recent reflection pointed directly towards incorporating a deeper understanding of spatial and relational information. That means an attention mechanism is the obvious next step.


  So, here''s the plan. I''ll craft a brand-new `create_network` function. I''m calling it `SokobanAttentionGRUCNN`. The idea is to slap a self-attention layer right after the convolutional feature extraction – before the GRU layer. This way, the network can selectively "pay attention" to the most relevant bits of the flattened CNN features. The GRU can then do its temporal processing on this focused representation. Simple, elegant, and hopefully effective. Oh, and I''ll stick with the best fixed hyper-parameters from Evaluation ID 28. No need to fix what isn''t broken! Let''s see if this pays off!

  '
