- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now submit a corrected implementation of the self-attention mechanism, applying it over the spatial locations of the CNN feature map to properly enhance structured reasoning. I will use the fixed best hyperparameters from Evaluation ID 28.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-SpatialAttention-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"rl, policy-gradient, cnn, gru, attention, agent-architecture, spatial-reasoning\"\nabstract: \"This submission corrects the implementation of the self-attention mechanism (MultiHeadDotProductAttention). Instead of attending over a single flattened feature vector, attention is now applied over spatial tokens derived from the CNN feature map. This aims to allow the network to explicitly focus on relevant game elements across the grid, improving spatial and relational reasoning for planning. Hyperparameters are fixed to the best performing values from Evaluation ID 28.\"\ncontent: |\n \
    \ import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters based on the best trial from Evaluation ID 28.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000259]),  # Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.011754]),   # Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.573199]),# Fixed to best from Eval ID 28\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),       # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),      # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'gru_features': tune.choice([256]),        # Fixed to best from previous trial\n          'attention_heads': tune.choice([4]),       # Number of attention heads\n          'attention_features':\
    \ tune.choice([128])   # Feature dimension for attention's qkv (e.g., cnn_features_2)\n      }\n\n  class SokobanSpatialAttentionGRUCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN with Spatial Attention and GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      gru_features: int\n      attention_heads: int\n      attention_features: int # Dimensionality for Q, K, V projections\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          \"\"\"Forward pass through the network.\"\"\"\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN Feature Extraction (with residual connections)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Reshape CNN output for spatial attention: (B, H, W, C) -> (B, H*W, C)\n          # Assuming x has spatial dimensions H, W and channels C_out = self.cnn_features_2\n          _, H, W, C_out = x.shape\n          spatial_tokens = x.reshape((batch_size, H * W, C_out))\n\n          # Apply MultiHeadDotProductAttention over spatial tokens\n          # queries, keys, and values are all spatial_tokens\
    \ for self-attention\n          attended_spatial_tokens = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(\n              num_heads=self.attention_heads,\n              qkv_features=self.attention_features,\n              out_features=C_out, # Output features should match input token features\n              name=\"spatial_attention_layer\"\n          )(spatial_tokens, spatial_tokens, spatial_tokens)\n          \n          # Flatten the attended spatial tokens for GRU input: (B, H*W, C_out) -> (B, H*W*C_out)\n          flattened_attended_features = attended_spatial_tokens.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n\n          # GRU Layer for temporal processing\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          \n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          new_rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, flattened_attended_features) # Input to GRU is now flattened attended features\n          \n          # Shared\
    \ MLP backbone after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Separate heads for policy and value\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          \n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-SpatialAttention-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return SokobanSpatialAttentionGRUCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          gru_features=hparams['gru_features'],\n          attention_heads=hparams['attention_heads'],\n          attention_features=hparams['attention_features']\n\
    \      )\n\n  # No override for create_optimizer or training_step; using defaults.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing the Attention Glitch**


  Okay, here I am at the Research Counter again. Damn, Eval ID 79 was a bust. I completely messed up the attention implementation. I was so focused on treating the CNN output as a single global vector, I forgot the whole point of using attention: to focus on *different spatial locations*. Facepalm.


  So, the next step is crystal clear: submit the corrected implementation. The key is to reshape that CNN output. It needs to be in a sequence format: `(batch_size, sequence_length, features_per_token)`. Think of `sequence_length` as the number of spatial locations, so that''s height times width, and `features_per_token` is the number of channels. Then, finally, I can apply `MultiHeadDotProductAttention` properly. It should be able to intelligently focus on different areas of the image.


  No need to reinvent the wheel with the hyperparameters; I''ll use the fixed best ones from Evaluation ID 28. Keep it simple, keep it efficient. Let''s get this one right.

  '
