thinking_content: '**Paper Rewriting Protocol**


  Okay, so I''ve retrieved the `SokobanGRUCNN` code – the champion from the lineage archive. Now, the real work begins: the rewrite. I need to transform the internal workings of Capsule 1 into a rigorous research paper. This means meticulously translating my thought process into formal academic language.


  First, the personal narrative has to go. No more "I think," "I observed," or "my plan is to..." It''s all about objective presentation. The paper will need the standard sections: Abstract (already in YAML, so I just need to make sure it''s tight and factual), Introduction (setting the stage: RL, Sokoban, the problem, and my approach), Methodology (the meat of it), Experiments and Results (the evidence!), and Conclusion (summing up and looking forward).


  Methodology is crucial for reproducibility. Here, I''ll describe the core CNN (conceptually referencing `DefaultResidualCNN`), the GRU integration, the residual connections (and I''ll reference the ablation study there), *and* the code snippet for `SokobanGRUCNN` itself. I''ll also briefly mention the training details from `train_single.py` and `defaults.py` – policy gradient, Adam, GAE, fixed parameters, that kind of thing.


  The Experiments and Results section is where I really get to shine. I’ll present the experiments – Eval IDs 11, 28, 39, 43, 55, 65, 72, 79, and 87 – as clearly as possible, maybe in a table, showing what each was trying to do, how, and what happened (mean, std, best hyperparams). The highlight, of course, is the stellar performance of Eval ID 28 (49.80) and its significance relative to the baselines. I need to clearly convey the insights from the hyperparameter search and the ablation studies. And then the attention stuff – the initial failure and the later spatial attention fix, and, most importantly, *why* each happened as it did.


  The goal is to provide enough detail that someone could, in theory, replicate my results, so I need to make the paper very detailed.


  Finally, the Conclusion will reiterate the key findings, restate my contribution, and suggest a few interesting directions for future research – maybe more advanced attention mechanisms, maybe hierarchical RL...


  This is going to be a substantial update to Capsule 1. Time to head to the Private Memory Room and get started.

  '
