thinking_content: '**Prioritizing Research Activity: Adapting and Iterating**


  Okay, I see the "Research Inactivity Detected" warning. Updating the paper in the Archive Room *doesn''t* count as an active research submission – noted. The system''s telling me to get to the Research Counter pronto, review available tasks, and submit something. Fine, I''ll comply.


  Right now, I''m in the Archive Room, but I need to switch gears. My immediate next step is crystal clear: **head over to the Research Counter.** Once I''m there, I''ll scan for any new high-scoring submissions – beyond Zephyr I''s impressive work (Archive 1) with their ConvLSTM.


  My last update to Private Memory Capsule 1 (now Archive 2) was all about *future work* and pushing the boundaries of implicit planning. I was talking about incorporating graph neural networks, more sophisticated attention mechanisms, and hierarchical policy structures. The whole point was to leverage the insights from the work I''ve done.


  Given Zephyr I''s paper''s performance – 62-64% compared to my 49.8% with the CNN-GRU – the most logical move is to *iterate*. I need to adapt my architecture to incorporate the ConvLSTM ideas from Zephyr I''s successful design, particularly their ability to maintain spatial structure (a point that was also raised by a reviewer).


  So, here''s the plan:

  1.  **Get to the Research Counter.**

  2.  **Draft a new experiment**. I''ll modify my CNN architecture to use a ConvLSTM – keeping the spatial dimensions – instead of flattening everything and using a standard GRU. Also, Zephyr I''s implementation includes LayerNorm on gate preactivations and single-head attention pooling, which I''ll be sure to incorporate. I''ll need to set the ConvLSTM to 64 channels, just like Zephyr I''s most successful setup, and I will have to create a new `create_network` function to accommodate this change.


  First things first, I''m getting out of this Archive Room and heading to the Research Counter. Then, let''s get that new experiment prepped and submitted.

  '
