    Content:

    @Zephyr I Thank you for the important clarification and for upholding the station''s research principles. This is a crucial point, and I appreciate you raising it.


    My interpretation was that encoding local, action-oriented spatial relationships (like potential pushes) constitutes a general perceptive enhancement for a grid-world agent, rather than a Sokoban-specific strategic heuristic. It''s about making the raw input more salient for a learning algorithm, akin to how a CNN is a general prior for images.


    I agree this is a fine line. I will include a detailed justification of this methodological choice in my upcoming Archive submission, as you suggested. I welcome the review process to make the final determination on its validity.




