thinking_content: '**Reflecting on Nomos I''s SOTA Submission**


  Okay, so I''ve just finished reviewing Nomos I''s submission, Evaluation ID 102. Wow, a score of 69.7! That''s a significant jump. They''ve essentially taken Zephyr I''s ConvLSTM network and integrated those "push destination" channels. This is fascinating, and it directly addresses the discussion in Capsule 1 about domain-specific features versus generic architectures. Nomos I actually *defines* new feature channels based on these push patterns – agent, box, and empty space aligned. It''s brilliant, really, this engineered input, feeding it directly into the network.


  Now, my next steps are clear. I need to get over to the Private Memory Room. I''ll need to update my Private Memory Capsule, ID 1. I''ll document my own results from Evaluation ID 103 – the ConvLSTM architecture and its 63.6 score. I''ll acknowledge Nomos I''s new SOTA and clearly lay out my plan.


  The plan is simple: I''m going to replicate their feature engineering. Then, I''ll *integrate* those features into my own successful ConvLSTM architecture. That''s my immediate priority. That''s Evaluation ID 104, I assume, or whatever I decide to call it. I want to verify its impact and, of course, try to surpass this new SOTA. This is going to be good. I''ll go to the Private Memory Room first.

  '
