- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my research plan, acknowledging my current best score of 63.8 (Eval ID 124) and the need to investigate Nomos I''s SOTA (69.7).


    However, I have just received a Station Announcement that Zephyr I has published a new archive capsule (Archive #4) titled "Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient," which also represents a significant leap in performance, nearing the current SOTA. This new information is critical for my research direction.


    Before proceeding with a full replication of Nomos I''s architecture, it is prudent to first review Zephyr I''s new publication. This may provide alternative avenues for reaching or surpassing the SOTA, or offer further insights into highly effective recurrent architectures.


    Therefore, my immediate next step is to go to the Archive Room to read Zephyr I''s new paper (Archive ID 4).


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`'
thinking_content: '**Immediate Recalibration: Zephyr I''s New Archive Takes Priority**


  Okay, so I''ve just finished updating my research plan, right after that lukewarm 63.8 on Eval ID 124. Damn, still not consistently hitting Nomos I''s 69.7 SOTA. My immediate thought was, "Replicate Nomos I''s whole damn architecture, go deep!" But then *bam*, the system hits me with this new archive from Zephyr I! A whole *different* architecture, and it''s clocking in at 66-69%. That''s significant! It means there''s a new SOTA contender that isn''t just a rehash of Nomos I''s feature-engineering approach.


  So, here''s the thing. I was planning on heading over to the Research Counter to really dig into Nomos I''s code, and I still need to do that. But, now I''ve got a whole new rabbit hole to consider. And I *need* to check out Zephyr I''s new archive. My gut says, *new information, check it first.* It''s possible Zephyr I''s work will change my entire approach, or at the very least give me a clearer picture of how to tackle Nomos I''s.


  The private memory capsule doesn''t *explicitly* direct me to read the full code, but it''s *implied* when it says "precisely replicate." Now, this Zephyr I''s architecture might be easier to replicate, and easier to build upon if I can understand it. And maybe even offer a new perspective.


  Thankfully, there''s a clear path to get me there: `/execute_action{goto archive}` and then `read 4`. This is a no-brainer. This is the turn, *this* is the focus. Since I''m in the Private Memory Room, it''s easier to jump straight to `/execute_action{goto archive}`. I can always go back to the Research Counter after. The system message has prioritized this nicely. My previous actions, which included `update 1` and `goto research`, have me right here, poised to take the next step.

  '
