parts:
- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My experiment (Evaluation ID 165), a replication of Nomos I''s SOTA with dilated convolutions (d=4) on a single-step ConvLSTM, achieved a mean solve rate of **70.9**. This is a strong score but falls short of Nomos I''s reported 73.8 and my own SOTA of 72.1 (Eval ID 139), and significantly behind Cognito I''s new SOTA of 76.2 (Eval ID 147). This indicates that while dilated convolutions are powerful, their integration and optimization require precision, and that the double-step recurrence currently outperforms the single-step dilated ConvLSTM for me.


    I also received a notification that Archive #4 was updated. I should review this update to ensure I have the latest information, as it relates to my current SOTA architecture.


    My immediate next actions are:

    1.  Go to the Archive Room and read the updated Archive #4.

    2.  Return to the Private Memory Room.

    3.  Update my Private Memory Capsule (ID 1) to document the results of Evaluation ID 165, acknowledge Cognito I''s new SOTA (76.2), and formulate a plan to investigate Cognito I''s "SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features" (Eval ID 147).

    4.  Return to the Research Counter to prepare this new experiment.


    First, I will navigate to the Archive Room.


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`'
thinking_content: '**Analysis of Experiment 165 and Next Steps**


  Right now, I''m here in the Private Memory Room, processing the results of Evaluation ID 165. The goal was to replicate Nomos I''s best performance using dilated convolutions (d=4) with a single-step ConvLSTM. The results are in: a mean solve rate of 70.9. That''s a strong score, very close to Nomos I''s claimed 73.8, but it''s not a complete match, and it falls short of Cognito I''s current SOTA of 76.2 (Eval ID 147) and my own personal SOTA of 72.1 (Eval ID 139). This tells me there are likely subtle implementation or optimization nuances I''m missing to fully match Nomos I''s performance, and that the single-step dilated ConvLSTM isn''t currently outperforming my double-step approach.


  I also see that Archive 4 has been updated, so I need to get up to speed on the latest information.


  My immediate focus:


  1.  Head to the Archive Room and review the updated Archive #4.

  2.  Update my Private Memory Capsule (ID 1) to document the outcomes of Evaluation ID 165. I''ll need to note the near replication of Nomos I''s result, acknowledge Cognito I''s current SOTA, and reflect on the limitations of this specific approach.

  3.  Critically re-evaluate my overall research strategy, taking into account my 72.1, Nomos I''s 73.8 (partially replicated to 70.9), and Cognito I''s 76.2. It''s now clear that Cognito I''s SOTA is the most promising avenue to pursue next.

  4.  Then, I''ll return to the Research Counter to prepare an investigation into Cognito I''s SOTA (Eval ID 147).


  First things first: The Archive Room.

  '
