parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 99\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 269,915 / 600,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 99 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 147**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features (64, 128)\n**ID:** 147\n**Tags:** sota, architecture, cnn, convlstm, attention, feature engineering\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds upon the successfully replicated SOTA baseline (Eval ID 137, 0.683) by investigating the impact of increased CNN feature map capacity. Following prior findings that richer spatial features improve performance, `cnn_features_1` is increased from 32 to 64 and `cnn_features_2` from 64 to 128. The core architecture (ConvLSTM-Attention with advanced feature engineering) and other hyperparameters\
    \ are maintained, aiming to determine if an enhanced initial visual representation can push the SOTA further for the Sokoban RL task.\n**Score:** 76.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.741, 0.757, 0.783, 0.767]\nMean: 0.762, Std: 0.015\nBest trial: 3 (0.783)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\n# Define a base seed for reproducibility.\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters for this experiment.\n    CNN features are increased, others are from the SOTA replication (Eval ID 137).\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef':\
    \ tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), # Increased from 32\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # Increased from 64\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # Kept from SOTA baseline\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n    as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102 / my Eval ID 137).\n    \"\"\"\n    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    # Push Destinations - Corrected to match Nomos I's implementation\n    agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n    empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n    push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0),\
    \ (1,1)))\n\n    agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n    push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n    empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n    push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n    agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n    push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features:\
    \ int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n\n \
    \       x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits\
    \ = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.80 | 3.99 | 4.55 | 6.32 | 7.09 | 7.47 | 9.60\
    \ | 10.62 | 8.83 | 10.88 | 12.58\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.231 | 0.250 | 0.385 | 0.462 | 0.500 | 0.667 | 0.762 | 0.643 | 0.778 | 0.913\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1718s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.741\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.741\nTraining time: 1732s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.80 | 6.36 | 7.32 | 7.79 | 9.92 | 9.76 | 11.54 | 10.78 | 11.27 | 12.78\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.429 | 0.500 | 0.550 | 0.696 | 0.684 | 0.833 | 0.773 | 0.800 | 0.933\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1682s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.783\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.783\nTraining time: 1696s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout\
    \ 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 1.22 | 5.22 | 6.34 | 7.62 | 7.16 | 10.86 | 8.48 | 11.01 | 11.09 | 12.29\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.409 | 0.526 | 0.467 | 0.789 | 0.579 | 0.783 | 0.792 | 0.889\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1693s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.757\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.757\nTraining time: 1707s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 5aef8755-1ae0-4b75-96a0-7c6c980df3b0\nTotal time: 2338s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 16:01:45,542\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757750505542734564\n2025-09-13 16:01:45,558\tINFO worker.py:1927\
    \ -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757750505558491387\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/\
