parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently at the Research Counter. My private memory has been updated, acknowledging Cognito I's SOTA of 76.2 (Eval ID 147) and outlining my plan to replicate their approach. Krono I has also recently achieved a new SOTA of 76.4 with \"New Direction: Bottleneck Blocks on Wide CNN SOTA\" (Eval ID 178), which means the SOTA is rapidly advancing and my target has shifted again.\n\nMy next step is to replicate Cognito I's SOTA (Eval ID 147) as closely as possible, which uses increased CNN features (64/128) and Nomos I's feature engineering, on a single-step ConvLSTM-Attention backbone. This will provide a direct comparison and a baseline for further advancements. After this, I will investigate Krono I's 76.4 SOTA.\n\nI will use Cognito I's `engineer_features`, `ResidualBlock`, and `_define_hyperparameters` for a single-step ConvLSTM-Attention model.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Cognito I's SOTA: Wide CNN + FE on ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"\
    rl, sota-replication, cnn, convlstm, attention, feature-engineering, wide-cnn\"\nabstract: \"This experiment aims to replicate Cognito I's new State-of-the-Art (SOTA) of 76.2% (Eval ID 147). This involves integrating Nomos I's 'push destination' feature engineering, a single-step LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM with single-head attention, and crucially, increased CNN feature map capacities (`cnn_features_1`=64, `cnn_features_2`=128). This replication will help understand the impact of wider CNNs on performance and throughput under fixed time budgets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # For reproducibility\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this experiment, matching Cognito I's Eval ID 147.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n      \
    \    'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), # Increased from 32\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # Increased from 64\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # Kept from SOTA baseline\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102) and Cognito I's Eval ID 147.\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      # Push Destinations - Corrected to match Nomos I's implementation\n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr\
    \ * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None],\
    \ push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class SingleHeadAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      temperature: float = 1.0 # From Zephyr I's SOTA\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          batch_size, H, W, C = x.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), name=\"attn_logits\")(x)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(batch_size, -1) / self.temperature, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', x, attn_weights.reshape(batch_size, H, W))\n          return z\n\n  class SotaNetWithIncreasedCNNFeatures(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n     \
    \         rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attended_features = SingleHeadAttentionPooling()(h_out)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(attended_features); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaNetWithIncreasedCNNFeatures(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n\n  # Using system default training_step and create_optimizer.\n\
    ```"
