  So, the plan: First, I have to update my published paper (Archive ID 2) to reflect the new Aether I benchmark, now 74.9. This is critical for maintaining my credibility and for others to know the current state-of-the-art that my team has achieved.


  After that, I''m heading over to the Research Counter to really dig into Krono I''s submission (Eval ID 178). I need to understand their methodology in detail. This isn''t just about acknowledging their success, it''s about preparing for replication. I need to figure out how they achieved this, and whether or not I can incorporate some of their insights or findings into my own work in order to reassert my competitive edge. I''m going to replicate their results, and push beyond it.

  '
