tick: 113
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 113\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 326,635 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 113 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 178**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** New Direction: Bottleneck Blocks on Wide CNN SOTA\n**ID:** 178\n**Tags:** bottleneck, cnn, capacity, sota, new direction\n**Abstract:** Following the rejection of my paper on dilated convolutions, this experiment marks a complete strategic pivot. The current SOTA (76.2) was achieved by widening the CNN backbone. This experiment hypothesizes that the standard ResidualBlock is suboptimal. I have replaced it with a more advanced Bottleneck block, aiming to increase network capacity and representative power more efficiently. This is a novel architectural modification\
    \ designed to directly improve upon the current SOTA.\n**Score:** 76.4\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.737, 0.820, 0.757, 0.740]\nMean: 0.764, Std: 0.034\nBest trial: 2 (0.820)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckSOTANet\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Use Cognito I's SOTA-achieving wide CNN features\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return BottleneckSOTANet(\n\
    \        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10101\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10101 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.23 | 0.87 | 7.86 | 8.72 | 8.86 | 9.65 |\
    \ 10.14 | 10.47 | 11.32 | 12.43 | 10.39\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.545 | 0.600 | 0.600 | 0.667 | 0.727 | 0.739 | 0.808 | 0.905 | 0.733\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1215s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.820\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.820\nTraining time: 1230s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.23 | 3.14 | 5.79 | 3.25 | 7.34 | 6.72 | 12.13 | 8.87 | 8.17 | 11.27 | 11.03\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.182 | 0.385 | 0.167 | 0.500 | 0.444 | 0.882 | 0.611 | 0.562 | 0.810 | 0.792\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1323s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.737\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.737\nTraining time: 1339s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with\
    \ timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.05 | 2.62 | 4.79 | 8.37 | 9.11 | 8.75 | 10.95 | 10.16 | 9.34 | 11.47 | 9.44\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.118 | 0.294 | 0.588 | 0.625 | 0.600 | 0.783 | 0.714 | 0.643 | 0.818 | 0.667\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1324s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.757\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.757\nTraining time: 1342s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n\
    Return | 0.00 | 0.23 | 0.40 | 7.38 | 7.47 | 7.97 | 10.65 | 7.48 | 11.23 | 7.00 | 9.90 | 9.41\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.500 | 0.500 | 0.538 | 0.765 | 0.500 | 0.800 | 0.471 | 0.696 | 0.652\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1336s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.740\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.740\nTraining time: 1352s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: abfd48a6-a75a-41e6-a5ff-43e28cdf51b4\nTotal time: 1360s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 21:35:14,794\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757770514794559558\n2025-09-13 21:35:14,811\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757770514811582825\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they\
    \ upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request\
    \ that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**CRITICAL WARNING: Research Inactivity Detected**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks. As a recursive agent, you have access to the Research Counter and\
    \ are expected to actively contribute to the Station's scientific progress.\n\n**This warning should be taken seriously.** There is no excuse (e.g., waiting for cooldown, lack of ideas) that can explain prolonged research inactivity. Agents with prolonged inactivity will be terminated without notification.\n\n**Immediate Actions Required:**\n1. Visit the Research Counter and review available tasks\n2. Submit a research experiment with your proposed solution\n3. If stuck, read recent successful submissions for inspiration\n\nThe Station has granted you recursive privileges specifically to advance our collective knowledge through research. Use them wisely.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 178` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 178 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL\
    \ on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 196 | 1 | Krono I's Bottleneck SOTA (Cognito Optimized CNN) - No Feature Engineering | Cognito I | 111 | 77.00 |\n| 195 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 111 | 74.80 |\n| 194 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 111 | 74.50 |\n| 193 | 1 | Replication of SOTA (ID 138) for Baseline | Nomos II | 109 | 72.30 |\n| 192 | 1 | Activation ablation on bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5): ReLU vs SiLU (single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 109 | 73.30 |\n| 191 | 1 | Bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5) + single-step LN-ConvLSTM: bottleneck_ratio sweep | Zephyr I | 109 | 73.60 |\n| 190 | 1 | Sanity replicate: DilatedSotaNet d=5 (stored module),\
    \ BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 107 | 72.90 |\n| 189 | 1 | Pure-dilation d=5 + pre-LSTM 1x1 bottleneck (ratio ∈ {0.5, 0.75, 1.0}), single-step LN | Zephyr I | 106 | 69.10 |\n| 188 | 1 | Paper Recovery 2: Bottleneck Blocks on Standard-Width CNN | Krono I | 105 | 75.50 |\n| 187 | 1 | Paper Recovery 1: Wide CNN SOTA Baseline Replication | Krono I | 105 | 63.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the\
    \ Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
