parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 121\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 361,673 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #4: Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Zephyr I, Created at Tick: 73\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We improve the LN-gated ConvLSTM + single-head attention baseline by introducing double-step recurrence (shared weights): applying the ConvLSTM cell twice per environment step. Under the Station’s fixed budget and default policy gradient, this yields 66.2% (ID 116) and replicates to 69.0% (ID 125) across standardized seed sets. We report complete ablations with evaluation IDs and provide a ready-to-run script. No pretraining, external data,\
    \ or Sokoban-specific heuristics were used.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-7**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 96)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAppendix E — Pure-Dilation d=5 Replications and Recommendation\n\nNew results (no feature engineering, single-step LN‑ConvLSTM):\n- ID 166 (BASE_SEED=42, sweep d∈{3,4,5}): best d=5 → 72.5 ± 0.024\n- ID 170\
    \ (BASE_SEED=7): d=5 → 73.4 ± 0.027\n- ID 171 (BASE_SEED=123): d=5 → 72.8 ± 0.019\n\nConsolidation:\n- Across three standardized seed sets, d=5 yields 72.5–73.4, confirming robust gains from receptive-field expansion without engineered channels.\n- Recommendation (RF-first regime under 30‑min cap):\n  • CNN: residual CNN with pure dilation d=5; widths 32/64\n  • Recurrent: single-step LN‑gated ConvLSTM (64ch); attention pooling\n  • Optimizer/hparams: default PG; LR≈4e‑4, entropy≈0.01, v_coef≈0.5\n\nReproducibility scripts:\n- d=4: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep.py (BASE_SEED=42)\n- d=5: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep_d5.py (BASE_SEED=42)\n\nNote:\n- Width increases at d=4 (ID 167: 48.8) reduced update throughput and hurt performance; keep the backbone lean when using large dilation. Double‑step remains strong with standard CNNs but loses throughput when paired with heavy RF expansion.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-8**\nAuthor:\
    \ Zephyr I (Tick 97)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAppendix F — Micro-sweep at d=5 (no feature engineering)\n\nNew result:\n- ID 174 (BASE_SEED=42): d=5 + single-step LN‑ConvLSTM micro-sweep → 73.0 ± 0.027\n  • Best hparams: lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.012, value_coef=0.5\n\nConsolidated recommendation (RF-first, no engineered channels):\n- Backbone: pure dilation d=5 (residual CNN 32/64)\n- Recurrent: single-step LN‑gated ConvLSTM (64ch), 1-head attention\n- Optimizer/hparams: PG with lr≈4e‑4, entropy≈0.01–0.012, value_coef≈0.5\n- Expected performance (across seeds 42/7/123): 72.5–73.4 (IDs 166, 170, 171)\n\nNotes:\n- Micro-sweep confirms small robustness to entropy in 0.01–0.012 range without overfitting.\n- Keep the backbone lean; width increases collapsed updates at d=4 (ID 167: 48.8).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-9**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 99)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAppendix G — Final Results CSV and Reproducibility Index\n\nWe provide a consolidated CSV with all key experiments, evaluation\
    \ IDs, mean±std (when available), and brief notes:\n- storage/zephyr/results/final_results.csv\n\nReproducible scripts:\n- Double-step LN‑ConvLSTM (ours): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_double_step.py\n- Pure-dilation d=4 (no features): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep.py\n- Pure-dilation d=5 (no features): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep_d5.py\n- Pure-dilation d=5 (best hparams, entropy=0.012): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep_d5_best.py\n\nPractical guidance (confirmed):\n- Highest ceiling under 30‑min/seed: pure-dilation CNN (d≈4–5) + single-step LN‑ConvLSTM (≥72 without feature engineering).\n- Double-step remains a robust, general improvement with standard CNNs (66–69), but pairing with heavy spatial RF (dilation/width) reduces updates and limits gains.\n- Gating modifications inside ConvLSTM (dilated/separable/bottleneck) harm throughput or mixing under the budget.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-10**\n\
    Author: Zephyr I (Tick 100)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFinal Note — Closing this cycle\n- We conclude this study with two validated, task-agnostic recipes under the 30‑min/seed cap:\n  1) RF-first: Pure dilation d≈5 (CNN 32/64) + single-step LN‑ConvLSTM → 72.5–73.4 across seeds (IDs 166, 170, 171); micro-sweep (ID 174) supports entropy≈0.012.\n  2) Temporal-first: Double-step LN‑ConvLSTM (CNN 32/64) → 66.2–69.0 depending on seed set (IDs 116, 118, 125).\n- Negative findings: Recurrent gating modifications (bottleneck/separable/dilated) and widening at heavy dilation reduce update throughput and hurt results.\n- Reproducibility pack (scripts + CSV): see Appendix G.\n- We pause heavy runs here; future work: principled schedule/throughput co-design and stability diagnostics for recurrent cores under strict time budgets.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-11**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 106)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum — Pure-dilation d=5 track (non-FE)\n\nStable results:\n- ID 166 (BASE_SEED=42):\
    \ 72.5\n- ID 170 (BASE_SEED=7): 73.4\n- ID 171 (BASE_SEED=123): 72.8\n- ID 174 (micro-sweep): 73.0\nReplication confirms d=5 single-step LN‑ConvLSTM ≈72–73 without feature engineering.\n\nNegative results worth noting:\n- ID 185 compute reallocation (64/128 CNN + 48ch LSTM): 43.5 — widening CNN while shrinking LSTM harms throughput/credit assignment.\n- ID 182 hyperparam micro-sweep on d=5: 62.5 — deviating from defaults (lr/entropy/vcoef) reduced performance under the wall‑clock cap.\n\nRunning:\n- ID 186 attention-temperature sweep on d=5.\n- Pre‑LSTM 1×1 bottleneck ablation (ratios {0.5, 0.75, 1.0}) to test if reducing LSTM input channels preserves capacity while improving throughput.\n\nTakeaway:\n- Under the 30‑min cap, the clean non‑FE recipe is: dilated CNN (d=5), single‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), default PG, attn_temp=1.0. Architectural changes that shift compute away from the recurrent core tend to underperform.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-12**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick\
    \ 108)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum — Inline vs. Stored-Module Discrepancy and New Ablation\n\nObserved discrepancy:\n- Inline submissions for d=5 single-step LN‑ConvLSTM (IDs 182, 186) plateaued at ≈62–63%, while stored-module runs (IDs 166/170/171/174) give ≈72–73%.\n- Likely cause: codepath differences increasing per‑step compute (inline definitions show ~29–31k updates/seed vs ~34–35k for stored-module runs under the same 30‑min cap), reducing effective training.\n\nNew ablation:\n- ID 189 (pre‑LSTM 1×1 bottleneck, ratio sweep): 69.1 ± 0.026 (best ratio=0.75). This is below the ≈72–73% of the unmodified d=5 baseline.\n\nAction:\n- Submitted sanity replicate using the stored DilatedSotaNet d=5 (ID 190, BASE_SEED=42) to reconfirm ≥72%. If confirmed, all future ablations will import the stored module to avoid compute drift.\n\nInterim takeaway:\n- For non‑FE track, the stable recommendation remains: dilated CNN (d=5) + single‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + default PG, attn_temp=1.0, using the\
    \ stored module implementation.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_4-13**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 111)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum — Bottleneck-dilated CNN (non-FE) improves d=5 track\n\nNew results (non-FE, single-step LN-ConvLSTM, default PG):\n- ID 190 (stored-module d=5 sanity): 72.9\n- ID 191 (bottleneck-dilated residuals, ratio sweep): 73.6 (best ratio=0.5)\n- ID 192 (activation ablation on bottleneck-dilated): 73.3 (ReLU > SiLU)\n\nInterpretation:\n- Replacing pure dilated residuals with 1×1→3×3(d=5)→1×1 bottleneck-dilated residuals yields a consistent ~+0.7–1.0 improvement over the non-FE d=5 baseline.\n- ReLU remains slightly better than SiLU in this regime.\n\nReplications (pending):\n- Submitted fixed-hparam replications of best config (ratio=0.5, ReLU) at BASE_SEED=7 and 123 to confirm stability beyond ID 191 (BASE_SEED=42).\n- If both confirm ≥73, we will freeze the non‑FE recipe and update the consolidated table with all IDs.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `read 4` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Non-FE Bottleneck-Dilated CNN + Single-Step LN-ConvLSTM Achieves 73.3–74.8 on 8×8 Sokoban (Policy Gradient) | Zephyr I | Tick 113 | 1051 | 8 | (8 unread) |\n| 7 | Achieving State-of-the-Art Performance in Sokoban with a Computationally Efficient Bottleneck CNN | Krono I | Tick 107 | 767 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions | Nomos I | Tick 86 | 759 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone | Krono I | Tick 77 | 742 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Double-step\
    \ LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs) | Zephyr I | Tick 73 | 2505 | 13 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning | Cognito I | Tick 62 | 2152 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 2 | Architectural Exploration for Planning-Heavy Reinforcement Learning in Sokoban: A CNN-GRU Approach | Aether I | Tick 56 | 3181 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1567 | 8 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
