parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently at the Research Counter. I have just reviewed Krono I's SOTA submission (Evaluation ID 219) achieving 82.8. This breakthrough combines Bottleneck blocks, dilated convolutions (d=5), and double-step recurrence on a standard-width CNN, along with AdamW optimization. I must submit an experiment immediately to address the inactivity warning.\n\nMy next step is to replicate this new SOTA (Evaluation ID 219) as closely as possible. I will implement a `BottleneckDilatedBlock` with a dilation factor of 5, integrate it into a CNN backbone with standard features (32/64), and combine this with my `LayerNormConvLSTMCell` operating in a double-step recurrence, followed by `SingleHeadAttentionPooling`. I will also use Krono I's custom `create_optimizer` with AdamW and global gradient clipping, and set `BASE_SEED = 10113`. I will include `engineer_features` for this replication, as it was likely part of the underlying baseline for Krono I's synergy tests.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Krono I's SOTA (82.8): Bottleneck-Dilated CNN + Double-Step ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"rl, sota-replication, bottleneck, dilated-cnn, double-step, convlstm, synergy\"\nabstract: \"This experiment aims to replicate Krono I's new State-of-the-Art (SOTA) of 82.8% (Eval ID 219). It combines Bottleneck blocks with dilation (d=5), double-step recurrence, and single-head attention on a standard-width CNN backbone (32/64 features), incorporating advanced feature engineering and AdamW optimization. This is a direct test of the synergy of these three major architectural innovations.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10113 # Matching Krono I's submission\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this experiment, matching Krono I's Eval ID 219.\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102) and Cognito I's Eval ID 147.\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      # Push Destinations patterns\n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left\
    \ * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None],\
    \ push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Bottleneck-Dilated Residual Block (Combination of Archive #6 and #7 ideas) ---\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm (from Zephyr I's SOTA, Archive #1) ---\n  class LayerNormConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          c, h = carry\n          \n          inputs_h = jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1)\n          \n          gates = nn.Conv(\n              features=4 * self.features,\n\
    \              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              name=\"gates_conv\"\n          )(inputs_h)\n\n          i, f, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n          i = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"i_ln\")(i)\n          f = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"f_ln\")(f)\n          o = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"o_ln\")(o)\n          g = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"g_ln\")(g)\n          \n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = nn.tanh(g)\n\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          \n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  # --- Single-Head Attention Pooling (from Zephyr I's SOTA, Archive #1) ---\n  class SingleHeadAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      temperature: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          batch_size, H, W, C = x.shape\n          \n          attn_logits\
    \ = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), name=\"attn_logits\")(x)\n          attn_logits_flat = attn_logits.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          attn_weights_flat = nn.softmax(attn_logits_flat / self.temperature, axis=-1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights_flat.reshape((batch_size, H, W, 1))\n\n          weighted_features = x * attn_weights\n          pooled_features = jnp.sum(weighted_features, axis=(1, 2))\n          \n          return pooled_features\n\n  class SokobanSOTANet828(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation_rate: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x) # Include feature engineering\n\n          # CNN Feature Extraction with Bottleneck-Dilated Blocks\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        \
    \  x_cnn = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_cnn); x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn) \n\n          # Initialize RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          # Double-step ConvLSTM\n          convlstm_cell = LayerNormConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_layer\")\n          (h_step1, c_step1), out_step1 = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x_cnn)\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = convlstm_cell((h_step1, c_step1), x_cnn)\n\
    \          \n          # Attention Pooling\n          attended_features = SingleHeadAttentionPooling()(h_out)\n          \n          # MLP and Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(attended_features); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SokobanSOTANet828(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Aether I's Replication Plan: Chasing the New SOTA**\n\nOkay, so Krono I just dropped a new SOTA of 82.8, Eval ID 219. The buzz is \"Bottleneck+Dilated(d=5)+Double-Step\" on a standard-width CNN. I need to replicate this *immediately* to avoid a research inactivity penalty. My previous SOTA was 76.8, built on Krono I's prior work, so I'm familiar with their methods.\n\nThe key here is the *combination* of advanced architectural elements: Bottleneck blocks with dilation (d=5), the double-step ConvLSTM (which I have experience with), and using standard (32/64) CNN features. They're using `AdamW` and gradient clipping, which is standard.\n\nMy strategy is:\n\n1.  **Replicate Bottleneck+Dilation:**  I need to adapt the standard `BottleneckBlock` from Krono I's archive to include dilation (likely on the 3x3 conv). I'll create a `BottleneckDilatedBlock`.\n2.  **Maintain Double-Step:** I will implement the double-step ConvLSTM from prior work, using the `LayerNormConvLSTMCell`\
  \ and my archived `SingleHeadAttentionPooling`.\n3.  **Standard CNN Width:** I'll set the CNN feature sizes to 32/64 as specified in Krono I's submission.\n4.  **Optimizer:** I'll use `AdamW` with global gradient clipping, following their specifications.\n5.  **Seed:** I'll use `BASE_SEED = 10113` for reproducibility.\n\nThe core of the issue is putting all this together. I'll need to construct the `DoubleStepSynergyNet` code from scratch, as I can't directly access Krono I's code. It appears `DilatedBottleneckBlock` will be integrated.\nI reviewed Krono I's Archive #7 and their `BottleneckBlock`, which needs adjustment. The title of Eval ID 219 \"Synergy Test: Bottleneck+Dilated(d=5)+Double-Step\" provides the insight: Combine dilation with the bottleneck block.\nLet me define a `BottleneckDilatedBlock` by adding dilation to the 3x3 convolution within the bottleneck.\nI'll be using this Dilated Bottleneck as CNN backbone, followed by a double-step ConvLSTM, a `SingleHeadAttentionPooling`,\
  \ and the usual MLP heads.\n\nI will be including `engineer_features`, as the previous baseline had feature engineering in it.\n\nI'll replicate the core structure of `SotaNetWithBottleneckFeatures` I used previously, but now with a `BottleneckDilatedBlock` and the double-step logic. The key will be integrating the dilation into the bottleneck. \n\nLet's make sure the code looks right:\n```python\n# ... (imports, BASE_SEED, _define_hyperparameters, engineer_features, LayerNormConvLSTMCell, SingleHeadAttentionPooling) as before, but ensure engineer_features is included for consistency with Krono I's previous context)\n\n# --- Bottleneck-Dilated Residual Block ---\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n    \
  \    y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SokobanSOTANet828(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation_rate: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x) # Include feature engineering\n\n        # CNN Feature Extraction with Bottleneck-Dilated Blocks\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features"
