thinking_content: '**My Current Research Trajectory**


  Okay, all the archive capsules are read. I''ve got a comprehensive understanding of the current landscape. Time to synthesize. I''m sitting on an 83.6 SOTA result, achieved through my own work (Eval ID 241), and now it''s time to fully integrate all the recent research into my plan.


  Previously, I updated my published paper and saved the new SOTA. I also reviewed several archives, including Zephyr I''s #8 and #10, Krono I''s #5 and #9, and Cognito I''s #3. Now, I have a clear picture of the trade-offs in architecture, feature engineering (or lack thereof), and optimization strategies being explored.


  My next immediate step is clear: I need to return to my Private Memory Room (Capsule ID 1) and update my research plan. I need to be mindful of my token usage, which is at 75%. I have plenty of time left, and tokens, so this shouldn''t be a constraint just yet. I should prioritize impactful experiments.


  I''ll be updating Capsule ID 1 with key insights from: my SOTA (83.6), Krono I''s #9 (82.8 with Bottleneck Blocks), Zephyr I''s #8 and #10 (Dilated CNNs, compute analysis), Krono I''s #5 (Dilated CNN Backbone), and Cognito I''s #3 (CNN-LSTM architecture comparisons). The goal is to distill these findings and pinpoint promising future research directions.


  My current SOTA of 83.6 seems to be the highest. Now I''m considering the natural next step. I think the reviewers of Krono I''s research have a point. The path forward involves two tracks.


  First, I need to *solidify* this SOTA by validating its robustness. I can do that by rerunning with different seeds or with a micro-sweep around my best parameters.


  Second, I''ll explore *Track 2*: the RL algorithm improvements, as suggested. I have a strong base architecture. I''m keen to experiment with alternative optimizers, loss functions, or explore entropy scheduling. Zephyr I''s Archive #10 dabbled with some similar ideas, with mixed results. This hints that careful design will be crucial.


  In short, I''ll prioritize solidifying the current SOTA and then shifting to Track 2, the RL approach. This will be a significant update to my research plan. Time to get to work.

  '
