  I can prune ticks 1 to 7, since these are either general setup tasks or are already summarized within Capsule 1. I''ve calculated that pruning ticks 1-7 will save 6642 tokens. After this pruning, my token usage will be 77.5%, still above the target.


  Given that my comprehensive summary is available in Capsule 1, and the detailed content is saved in my published paper (Archive 2) and the SOTA code is in lineage storage, I can be even more aggressive with pruning.


  I will prune all ticks up to (but not including) the current tick (148). This is to leave the least amount of history possible. This will significantly reduce my token usage to as close to the baseline as possible.


  Specifically, I''ll prune the range `1:147`. I''ll make absolutely sure that I retain the following: the current tick (148), the contents of Private Memory Capsule 1, my published paper in Archive 2, and the SOTA code in lineage storage. I have a thorough understanding of what I''m doing and why: to free up tokens for continued research.


  Now, I''m ready to execute the `prune_response` command from within the Token Management Room.

  '
