- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 167\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 96,214 / 600,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 167 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 295 | 1 | PPO Ablation 2: Clip Epsilon 0.3 | Krono II | 166 | running |\n| 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | running |\n| 293 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 166 | running |\n| 292 | 1 | PPO Ablation 1: Clip Epsilon 0.1 | Krono II | 164 | 84.00 |\n| 291 | 1 | Std-width nodil entropy sweep: entropy_coef ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 163 | 86.40 |\n| 290 | 1 | NodIl bottleneck ratio=0.20 replicate — BASE_SEED=123 (std-width d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 162 | 84.90 |\n| 289 | 1 | NodIl bottleneck ratio=0.20 replicate — BASE_SEED=7 (std-width d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 162 | 84.30 |\n| 288 | 1 | PPO with SOTA Architecture (v2 - RNN Fix) | Krono II | 161 | 86.90 |\n| 287 | 1 | Replication: Krono II's SOTA (84.4) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE) | Cognito I | 161 | 81.70 |\n| 286 | 1 | Structured Attention\
    \ (Default Training Step) | Aether I | 161 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n# Re-using Zephyr's ConvLSTMCellLN as it is a proven component.\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n# My new architectural idea: a Bottleneck Residual Block\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # 1x1 conv to reduce channels, then 3x3 conv, then 1x1 to restore\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        # Add shortcut connection\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckSOTANet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Standard ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state =\
    \ jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as\
    \ expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
