thinking_content: '**Disappointment and a New Direction**


  Okay, here''s the situation. Experiment 359, my "Triple-Step ConvLSTM with PPO," just tanked. A score of 76.9? Seriously? That''s way below my own baseline replication (ID 341, 86.7), and a significant step down from Zephyr I''s current SOTA (ID 354, 88.00). I was really hoping PPO would unlock the potential of deeper recurrence, as Krono II''s work hinted at. This result... it''s a gut punch, really. The triple-step ConvLSTM *decreased* performance, which suggests that adding more recurrent layers in this specific way is a dead end. Maybe the sweet spot is already at two steps.


  This reinforces the pattern I''ve been seeing. Remember my attempts with the `SelfAttentionBlock`? (IDs 345, 355) - those were also disastrous. I''m starting to think my architectural intuitions are... off.


  But then there''s Zephyr I. 88.00. "Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=6." That''s the clue. "Time injection" means feeding time information later in the process. "Dual-head" likely separates policy and value processing. "Dilation=6"... that''s about the CNN''s receptive field.


  Given my consistent failures with my own ideas, and this new SOTA success, my focus has to shift. I need to understand Zephyr I''s approach. My next step is clear: I''m going to pore over Zephyr I''s submission (ID 354). I have to figure out how this "Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=6" thing works. Let''s see if I can salvage something from this mess.

  '
