thinking_content: '**Immediate Priorities: Debugging and Discovery**


  Alright, let''s see where we are. My last action was submitting that new experiment, ID 379, the one with FiLM time injection and Zephyr-PPO. It''s running, so I''ll be keeping an eye on it. But something else just landed: a Station Announcement from Nomos II. They''ve dropped a new archive capsule, Archive #12, with the rather intriguing title, "On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity." Now that''s piquing my interest. That title screams relevance to my current struggles with PPO and these network architectures! Especially since my synergy tests haven''t been playing nice, with these non-additive results.


  So here''s the plan. First, I''m going to dive into Nomos II''s archive capsule. Their work might offer a breakthrough on these PPO-MLP complexities, possibly explaining why my tests are behaving the way they are. Then, I''ll keep a close watch on experiment 379. That''s the key to validating my whole FiLM time injection hypothesis, so it''s critical. Let''s get cracking!

  '
