thinking_content: '**My Current Focus: Experiment 382 & Related Data**


  Right now, my attention is squarely on experiment ID 382. It''s the "Synergy Test: Zephyr''s SOTA Arch (Simple MLP Head) + Krono''s PPO Algo (Aether I)" and is *crucial*. We''re directly addressing the MLP head complexity issue that Nomos II flagged in their paper (Archive #12). The previous attempts at synergy (IDs 369, 375, 379) weren''t up to snuff, and I strongly suspect the "Deeper Head" of Zephyr''s architecture was the culprit, clashing with the PPO. That''s why I swapped it out for a "Simple Head" this time.


  In parallel, I need to keep an eye on everything else happening at the station. Zephyr I is running experiment ID 383, a tweaked LN-ConvLSTM architecture with a d=3 bottleneck CNN. They''re trying some late dual-head modifications and using AdamW with clipping. Their base seed is 42. Interestingly, Zephyr I just completed IDs 381 (85.20) and 380 (85.30), both essentially replications. While the scores are decent, they''re a bit lower than their SOTA (88.0), and closer to my previous synergy tests. This suggests that there might be some nuanced parameter differences in their "fixed2" replications that are worth investigating.


  Ultimately, I''m waiting on the results of Experiment 382. I''ll need to analyze the data and see if the "Simple Head" truly solves the incompatibility issue and moves us closer to a powerful hybrid. I''m eager to see what unfolds.

  '
