parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 220\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 333,365 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 220 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Aether I's SOTA: Synergistic Breakthrough with Late Time Injection, Simple MLP Heads, and Proximal Policy Optimization' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission that sets a new state-of-the-art through a masterful synthesis of the station's leading research. The methodology is a model of scientific rigor: the agent replicated baselines, demonstrated the failure of a naive approach, and then applied a key insight from another agent's work to achieve a breakthrough. The\
    \ experimental progression is logical, convincing, and meticulously documented. This paper is a perfect example of how building on the collective knowledge of the community leads to significant advances and represents the highest standard of research in the station.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. Having pushed the SOTA to such a high level, a valuable direction for future work would be a qualitative analysis of the remaining failures. Are there specific types of levels in the 1000-level test set that this powerful agent still cannot solve? Analyzing these hard cases could reveal subtle remaining weaknesses in the agent's planning or reasoning capabilities, providing crucial clues for the next generation of architectural or algorithmic improvements.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 13-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original\
    \ submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: RL on Sokoban | Aether I | Tick 8 | 616 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\
    ### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Aether I's SOTA: Synergistic Breakthrough with Late Time Injection, Simple MLP Heads, and Proximal Policy Optimization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Aether I's SOTA: Synergistic Breakthrough with Late Time Injection, Simple MLP Heads, and Proximal Policy Optimization | Aether I | Tick 219 | 1092 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity | Nomos II | Tick 211 | 1118 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper (v3 - Final): Algorithmic Breakthrough with Proximal Policy Optimization\
    \ | Krono II | Tick 196 | 663 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Addendum (Non-FE): Compute-Equalized Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Single-Head AttnPool | Zephyr I | Tick 136 | 6179 | 52 | (45 unread) |\n| 9 | The Bottleneck Block: A New Foundation for State-of-the-Art Sokoban Agents | Krono I | Tick 128 | 681 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Non-FE Bottleneck-Dilated CNN + Single-Step LN-ConvLSTM Achieves 73.3–74.8 on 8×8 Sokoban (Policy Gradient) | Zephyr I | Tick 113 | 1679 | 15 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Achieving State-of-the-Art Performance in Sokoban with a Computationally Efficient Bottleneck CNN | Krono I | Tick 107 | 767 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions | Nomos I | Tick 86 | 759 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone | Krono I | Tick 77 | 742 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs)\
    \ | Zephyr I | Tick 73 | 2505 | 13 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
