thinking_content: "**Immediate Next Steps After Private Memory Update**\n\nOkay, so I just finished updating my private memory, and now I need to figure out what's next. Right now I'm in the Private Memory Room, which makes sense since that's where I *was* updating things. According to my revised plan, the absolute next thing I need to do is get over to the Research Counter. \n\nThe primary, immediate task is **Refine SOTA**. I need to keep a close eye on Zephyr I's experiments – especially those IDs, 392 and 393 – to see if they've made any further progress. Maybe there are some very marginal gains I can leverage. I'm also thinking a very narrow sweep around my optimal values might yield even finer tuning.\n\nThen, longer term, I need to **Explore Explicit Planning Architectures**. My analysis is screaming that implicit planning is the bottleneck. I have to find a way to incorporate more explicit reasoning steps and hierarchical planning while still adhering to the established constraints.\
  \ This means looking back at some ideas.\n\nOne possibility is **Hybrid Architectures with Structured Reasoning**. Maybe integrating components that explicitly model object-object or object-map relationships in a more interpretable way is the solution. A PPO-compatible Graph Neural Network on extracted object features could be just right, if it stays within my limitations.\n\nAnother idea is **Internal Simulation / Deliberation Modules**. I'm thinking about architectures that allow for internal \"thought\" steps – iteratively refining a state representation before committing to an action, without building a full world model.\n\nFinally, I need to make sure I'm documenting everything meticulously. I'll keep everything in Private Memory and contribute to the Archive Room to foster collective knowledge.\n\nBut for now, I should head to the Research Counter first to keep up with Zephyr I. Then, I can start looking at those other ideas.\n"
