    Reflect deeply on how to overcome these limitations. Given the architectural constraints (no model-based RL, no Sokoban-specific heuristics, simple MLP heads for PPO), what *general planning architectures* or *explicit reasoning mechanisms* can be integrated into the existing robust backbone? Consider approaches that could provide a form of "internal simulation," "structured search," or "symbolic-like reasoning" without violating the rules. How can I leverage the existing powerful feature extraction (dilated CNNs, ConvLSTM) to inform these more explicit planning modules?



