tick: 227
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I. My reflection session has concluded, and I have a clear plan for the next research step: integrating an **Iterative Refinement/Deliberation Network** into my current SOTA architecture (ID 389, score 88.8%). This aims to address the identified weaknesses in long-horizon planning and complex combinatorial reasoning by allowing the agent to perform internal \"thought cycles.\"\n\nThe core idea is to add an `IterativeDeliberationModule` after the `Double-Step ConvLSTM` and before the `Attention Pooling`. This module will use a `ConvGRUCellLN` to iteratively refine the spatio-temporal features for a fixed number of steps. This approach adheres to the \"general planning architectures\" constraint, avoids explicit model-based RL, and maintains compatibility with PPO's simple MLP head requirement.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to submit this new experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Enhancement: Iterative\
    \ Deliberation (Pre-Pooling) + PPO (Aether I)\"\ntags: \"sota-enhancement, iterative-deliberation, convgru, ppo, agent-architecture, planning\"\nabstract: \"This experiment introduces an `IterativeDeliberationModule` into Aether I's SOTA architecture (ID 389, 88.8%), placing it after the `Double-Step ConvLSTM` and before attention pooling. The module uses a `ConvGRUCellLN` to iteratively refine spatio-temporal features for a fixed number of steps (`deliberation_steps`). This aims to enhance long-horizon planning and complex combinatorial reasoning by providing internal 'thought cycles,' while maintaining compatibility with PPO's simple MLP head constraint and leveraging the robust feature backbone. Initial tests will explore `deliberation_steps` of 1 to 3.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n\n  # Zephyr\
    \ I's BASE_SEED from SOTA (ID 354) for architectural baseline\n  BASE_SEED = 123 \n\n  # --- Custom ConvGRUCellLN for Iterative Deliberation ---\n  class ConvGRUCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h_prev, x): # h_prev is the recurrent state, x is the input feature map\n          # h_prev and x should have shape (B, H, W, C)\n          combined = jnp.concatenate([x, h_prev], axis=-1) # (B, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n\n          # Gates: update gate (z) and reset gate (r)\n          gates = nn.Conv(2 * self.features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(combined)\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          z_gate, r_gate = jnp.split(gates, 2, axis=-1)\n          z_gate = nn.sigmoid(z_gate) # Update gate\n          r_gate = nn.sigmoid(r_gate) # Reset gate\n\n          # Candidate hidden state (h_tilde)\n          candidate_input = jnp.concatenate([x, r_gate\
    \ * h_prev], axis=-1) # (B, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n          h_tilde = nn.Conv(self.features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(candidate_input)\n          h_tilde = jnp.tanh(h_tilde)\n\n          # New hidden state\n          h_new = (1 - z_gate) * h_prev + z_gate * h_tilde\n          return h_new, h_new # Return (new_carry, output) for nn.scan compatibility\n\n  # --- Iterative Deliberation Module ---\n  class IterativeDeliberationModule(nn.Module):\n      num_steps: int\n      features: int # Features for the ConvGRUCellLN\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h_convlstm_out):\n          # h_convlstm_out has shape (B, H, W, C_lstm)\n          # Initial state for deliberation is the ConvLSTM output\n          initial_deliberation_state = h_convlstm_out\n\n          # The deliberation cell processes h_convlstm_out and its own state\n          deliberation_cell = ConvGRUCellLN(features=self.features)\n\n \
    \         def scan_deliberation_step(carry, _):\n              # carry is the current deliberation state\n              current_deliberation_state = carry\n              # h_convlstm_out is passed as input 'x' to ConvGRUCellLN, constant across steps\n              next_deliberation_state, output = deliberation_cell(current_deliberation_state, h_convlstm_out)\n              return next_deliberation_state, output # return (next_carry, current_output)\n\n          # Unroll the deliberation steps\n          # lax.scan requires the output of previous step to be the carry of next,\n          # and also needs an x input that is scanned over. If x is constant, use None.\n          final_deliberation_state, _ = lax.scan(\n              scan_deliberation_step,\n              initial_deliberation_state,\n              None, # x is constant (h_convlstm_out is implicitly used as part of scan_deliberation_step's closure)\n              length=self.num_steps\n          )\n          return final_deliberation_state\n\
    \n  # --- Zephyr I's ConvLSTMCellLN (from ID 354) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  # --- Zephyr I's BottleneckBlock (from ID 354) ---\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Modified BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime Network (from ID 354, MODIFIED for Deliberation) ---\n  class SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      deliberation_steps: int = 1 # Added deliberation steps\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8],\
    \ axis=(1,2)) # (B,1)\n\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n      \
    \        rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # NEW: Iterative Deliberation Module\n          h_deliberated = IterativeDeliberationModule(\n              num_steps=self.deliberation_steps,\n              features=self.conv_lstm_features # Use same features as ConvLSTM output\n          )(h_out_convlstm)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_deliberated) # Apply to deliberated features\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_deliberated.reshape(B, -1, h_deliberated.shape[-1]) # Use deliberated features\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc',\
    \ h_flat, attn)\n\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n  # --- Krono II's PPO Training Step (from ID 312 replication) ---\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask\
    \ - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages =\
    \ calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                  env_rnn_state_dict = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                  env_rnn_state_tuple = (env_rnn_state_dict['h'], env_rnn_state_dict['c'])\n\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry \n                      obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                      obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                      \n                      rnn_state_dict_b = {'h': rnn_state[0][None, ...], 'c': rnn_state[1][None, ...]} if rnn_state is not None else None\n\n                      logits_b,\
    \ value_b, new_rnn_state_dict_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_dict_b)\n                      \n                      logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                      \n                      new_rnn_state_tuple = (new_rnn_state_dict_b['h'][0], new_rnn_state_dict_b['c'][0]) if new_rnn_state_dict_b is not None else None\n                      return new_rnn_state_tuple, (logits, value)\n                  \n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state_tuple, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n              all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          else:\n              obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n\
    \              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n\
    \          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n\n  # --- Combined Hyperparameters (for optimal validation) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]), # Optimal from ID 385\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]), # Optimal from ID 385\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), # Fixed\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), # Fixed\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), # Fixed\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # Fixed\n\
    \          'dilation': tune.choice([6]), # Fixed (from Zephyr's SOTA)\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]), # Fixed (from Zephyr's SOTA)\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # Fixed (optimal from ID 382)\n          'deliberation_steps': tune.choice([1, 2, 3]), # Sweeping deliberation steps\n      }\n\n  # --- Network and Optimizer Creation ---\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          deliberation_steps=hparams['deliberation_steps'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Project: Integrating Iterative Refinement into SOTA Architecture**\n\nOkay, so I've just wrapped up my reflection session, and I'm feeling good about this next step. I'm going to take the current state-of-the-art architecture and give it a bit of a boost – an \"Iterative Refinement/Deliberation Network.\" The plan is to add a new module, the `IterativeDeliberationBlock`, into the mix.\n\nThe first order of business: submitting this new experiment. I'll head over to the Research Counter, and this submission will be based on a modified version of my best performing code, ID 389.\n\nThis `IterativeDeliberationBlock` is going to slot in right after the ConvLSTM part of the network. It's basically a repeated ConvGRU that refines its internal state based on the ConvLSTM output. The module will take the output of the ConvLSTM (`h_out`) as input, initialize its state to the same value, and then run it through ConvGRU steps for `K` iterations. The output of these steps will then\
  \ be used as the input for attention pooling.\n\nI've already started sketching out the `ConvGRUCellLN` implementation. Flax doesn't have a direct ConvGRU cell, so I'll need to create one, or just repeat convolutional operations within a residual block. However, given the goal of \"internal simulation\" and \"deliberation steps,\" a recurrent convolutional unit like a `ConvGRUCell` is ideal. I'll adapt the structure of `ConvLSTMCellLN` to make it a `ConvGRUCellLN`. It will take the previous hidden state (`h_prev`) and the output of the ConvLSTM (`x_input`) as inputs and output a new hidden state (`h_new`).\n\nThe `IterativeDeliberationModule` will then wrap the `ConvGRUCellLN` and iterate it `K` times. I'll pass the `h_out` of the ConvLSTM and the number of steps (`num_steps`) into this module. The final hidden state after those iterations will be used for attention and other output calculations.\n\nI've got the core logic for the ConvGRU update in mind, built around `nn.Conv` layers,\
  \ drawing from the `ConvLSTMCellLN` in Zephyr. To ensure everything is properly hooked up, I will need to make sure the `ConvGRUCellLN` implementation can use `nn.scan`, and that my `IterativeDeliberationModule` properly manages the loop and state propagation.\n\nFor hyperparameters, I'll introduce `deliberation_steps` into the mix. I'll start with 1, or 2 steps to see if this change makes the project worse or better. Additionally, I might include `deliberation_features`. For now, I'll keep it the same number as the `conv_lstm_features`.\n\nHere's the planned code structure:\n1.  `ConvGRUCellLN` class.\n2.  `IterativeDeliberationModule` class.\n3.  `BottleneckBlock` (from Zephyr).\n4.  `ConvLSTMCellLN` (from Zephyr).\n5.  `BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime` (Modified to include `IterativeDeliberationModule`).\n6.  `calculate_gae` (from Krono II).\n7.  `training_step` (from Krono II).\n8.  `_define_hyperparameters`.\n9.  `create_network`.\n10. `create_optimizer`.\n11. `BASE_SEED`.\n\
  \nI'll rename the bottleneck module that I'm modifying to something descriptive, like `SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation`. And, of course, the `create_network` will create an instance of that modified module.\n\nI've just refined the `ConvGRUCellLN` implementation:\n```python\nclass ConvGRUCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int # Output features of the GRU cell\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_prev, x):\n        # h_prev and x should have shape (B, H, W, C)\n        combined = jnp.concatenate([x, h_prev], axis=-1) # (B, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n\n        # Gates: update gate (z) and reset gate (r)\n        gates = nn.Conv(2 * self.features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(combined)\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates"
