role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 228\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 361,127 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 228 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (Pre-Pooling) + PPO (Aether I)' (ID: 403) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent\
    \ call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/storage/system/main.py\", line 464, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/storage/system/main.py\", line 440, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/storage/system/main.py\", line 322, in simple_cpu_validation\n    outputs = network.apply(params, dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py\", line 146, in __call__\n    h_deliberated = IterativeDeliberationModule(\n                  \
    \  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py\", line 62, in __call__\n    final_deliberation_state, _ = lax.scan(\n                                  ^^^^^^^^^\njax.errors.UnexpectedTracerError: Encountered an unexpected tracer. A function transformed by JAX had a side effect, allowing for a reference to an intermediate value with type float32[3,3,128,128] wrapped in a DynamicJaxprTracer to escape the scope of the transformation.\nJAX transformations require that functions explicitly return their outputs, and disallow saving intermediate values to global state.\nThe function being traced when the value leaked was scan_deliberation_step at /mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:52 traced for scan.\n------------------------------\nThe leaked intermediate value was created on line /mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:22:16\
    \ (ConvGRUCellLN.__call__). \n------------------------------\nWhen the value was created, the final 5 stack frames (most recent last) excluding JAX-internal frames were:\n------------------------------\n/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/storage/system/main.py:321:13 (simple_cpu_validation)\n/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:146:24 (SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation.__call__)\n/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:62:38 (IterativeDeliberationModule.__call__)\n/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:56:46 (IterativeDeliberationModule.__call__.<locals>.scan_deliberation_step)\n/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/99c049ba-2731-478c-8d76-0e67550b2d53/submission.py:22:16\
    \ (ConvGRUCellLN.__call__)\n------------------------------\n\nTo catch the leak earlier, try setting the environment variable JAX_CHECK_TRACER_LEAKS or using the `jax.checking_leaks` context manager.\nSee https://docs.jax.dev/en/latest/errors.html#jax.errors.UnexpectedTracerError\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (Pre-Pooling) + PPO (Aether I)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 403.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 405 | 1 | HParam Tuning on SOTA LSTM | Kairos I | 227 | 35.90 |\n| 404 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Graph-on-Grid GNN with SOTA Backbone | Nomos II | 227 | running |\n| 403 | 1 | SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (Pre-Pooling) + PPO (Aether I) | Aether I | 227 | n.a. |\n| 402 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 86.10 |\n| 401 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=7\
    \ — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 83.30 |\n| 400 | 1 | GRU + Policy Gradient | Kairos I | 224 | 40.30 |\n| 399 | 1 | Head ablation (time): GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 224 | 71.80 |\n| 398 | 1 | Insight I: CNNLSTM Baseline with Adjusted Hyperparameters | Insight I | 223 | 39.40 |\n| 397 | 1 | Head ablation: GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (no time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 223 | 66.00 |\n| 396 | 1 | SOTA Micro-Sweep: Zephyr's Arch (Simple Head) + PPO - Fine-tuned Hparams (Aether I) | Aether I | 223 | 87.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
