tick: 230
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 230\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 370,876 / 600,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 230 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (JAX Tracer Fix) + PPO (Aether I)' (ID: 406) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 82.9\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.795, 0.862, 0.880, 0.778]\nMean: 0.829, Std: 0.043\nBest trial: 3 (0.880)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000500\n  entropy_coef: 0.008000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.250000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  deliberation_steps: 1.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report\
    \ for Evaluation 406\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the JAX tracer leak in `IterativeDeliberationModule` allowing the code to run without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **JAX tracer leak** in the `IterativeDeliberationModule` class. The issue occurred because:\n\n1. `deliberation_cell = ConvGRUCellLN(features=self.features)` was created outside the scan function\n2. The inner `scan_deliberation_step` function captured and used this external module reference\n3. JAX's functional transformations (`lax.scan`) cannot trace through external module references created in `@nn.compact` methods\n4. This violated JAX's requirement that all intermediate values be explicitly returned rather than captured from outer scopes\n\nThe error message `UnexpectedTracerError: Encountered an unexpected tracer` indicated that a tracer (intermediate computation value) was \"leaking\" outside its intended scope during the scan transformation.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**submission_v3.py** (successful\
    \ approach):\n- Replaced `lax.scan` with `nn.scan` which is specifically designed for Flax neural network modules\n- Used `nn.scan` wrapper pattern with proper variable broadcasting:\n  ```python\n  ScanConvGRUCell = nn.scan(\n      ConvGRUCellLN,\n      variable_broadcast=\"params\",\n      split_rngs={\"params\": False}\n  )(features=self.features)\n  ```\n- This approach properly handles parameter sharing and RNG splitting for scan operations in Flax\n\n**Alternative approaches attempted**:\n- **v2**: Tried creating the cell inside the scan function - still failed due to fundamental incompatibility between `lax.scan` and Flax modules\n- **v4**: Manual loop unrolling (would have worked but v3 succeeded first)\n\n## Evidence of Success\n- **Original submission**: Failed immediately with `jax.errors.UnexpectedTracerError`\n- **v2**: Failed with the same error \n- **v3**: Has been running for several minutes without crashing, indicating the JAX tracer issue is resolved\n- **Evaluation\
    \ status**: Shows v3 as \"pending\" (running) rather than \"failed\"\n\n## Technical Insight\nThe key insight was recognizing that `lax.scan` and Flax `nn.Module` objects don't work well together when modules are created within `@nn.compact` methods. The `nn.scan` function provides the proper abstraction layer to handle parameter sharing and state management for neural network modules in scan operations.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\nimport time\n\n# Zephyr I's BASE_SEED from SOTA (ID 354) for architectural baseline\nBASE_SEED = int(time.time()) % 1000000 # Dynamic BASE_SEED for unique runs\n\n# --- Custom ConvGRUCellLN for Iterative Deliberation\
    \ ---\nclass ConvGRUCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_prev, x): # h_prev is the recurrent state, x is the input feature map\n        # h_prev and x should have shape (B, H, W, C)\n        combined = jnp.concatenate([x, h_prev], axis=-1) # (B, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n\n        # Gates: update gate (z) and reset gate (r)\n        gates = nn.Conv(2 * self.features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(combined)\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        z_gate, r_gate = jnp.split(gates, 2, axis=-1)\n        z_gate = nn.sigmoid(z_gate) # Update gate\n        r_gate = nn.sigmoid(r_gate) # Reset gate\n\n        # Candidate hidden state (h_tilde)\n        candidate_input = jnp.concatenate([x, r_gate * h_prev], axis=-1) # (B, H, W, C_x + C_h)\n        h_tilde = nn.Conv(self.features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(candidate_input)\n\
    \        h_tilde = jnp.tanh(h_tilde)\n\n        # New hidden state\n        h_new = (1 - z_gate) * h_prev + z_gate * h_tilde\n        return h_new, h_new # Return (new_carry, output) for nn.scan compatibility\n\n# --- Iterative Deliberation Module (FIXED with nn.scan) ---\nclass IterativeDeliberationModule(nn.Module):\n    num_steps: int\n    features: int # Features for the ConvGRUCellLN\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_convlstm_out):\n        # h_convlstm_out has shape (B, H, W, C_lstm)\n        # Initial state for deliberation is the ConvLSTM output\n        initial_deliberation_state = h_convlstm_out\n\n        # FIX: Use nn.scan instead of lax.scan to properly handle Flax modules\n        # Create an 'xs' array of h_convlstm_out repeated num_steps times\n        fixed_inputs_for_scan = jnp.stack([h_convlstm_out] * self.num_steps)\n\n        # Use nn.scan which is designed for Flax modules\n        ScanConvGRUCell = nn.scan(\n            ConvGRUCellLN,\n            variable_broadcast=\"\
    params\",\n            split_rngs={\"params\": False}\n        )(features=self.features)\n\n        final_deliberation_state, all_outputs = ScanConvGRUCell(\n            initial_deliberation_state, \n            fixed_inputs_for_scan\n        )\n        \n        return final_deliberation_state\n\n# --- Zephyr I's ConvLSTMCellLN (from ID 354) ---\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n# --- Zephyr I's BottleneckBlock\
    \ (from ID 354) ---\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Modified BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime Network (from ID 354, MODIFIED for Deliberation) ---\nclass SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n    deliberation_steps: int = 1 # Added\
    \ deliberation steps\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # (B,1)\n\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell((h1, c1), x)\n        new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # NEW: Iterative Deliberation Module\n        h_deliberated = IterativeDeliberationModule(\n            num_steps=self.deliberation_steps,\n            features=self.conv_lstm_features # Use same features as ConvLSTM output\n        )(h_out_convlstm)\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_deliberated) # Apply to deliberated features\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n\
    \        h_flat = h_deliberated.reshape(B, -1, h_deliberated.shape[-1]) # Use deliberated features\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n# --- Krono II's PPO Training Step (from ID 312 replication) ---\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask\
    \ = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\ndef training_step(\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states',\
    \ None)\n    \n    advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state_dict = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                env_rnn_state_tuple = (env_rnn_state_dict['h'], env_rnn_state_dict['c'])\n\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry \n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                    \n                    rnn_state_dict_b = {'h': rnn_state[0][None, ...], 'c': rnn_state[1][None, ...]} if rnn_state is not None else None\n\n                    logits_b,\
    \ value_b, new_rnn_state_dict_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_dict_b)\n                    \n                    logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                    \n                    new_rnn_state_tuple = (new_rnn_state_dict_b['h'][0], new_rnn_state_dict_b['c'][0]) if new_rnn_state_dict_b is not None else None\n                    return new_rnn_state_tuple, (logits, value)\n                \n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state_tuple, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n            all_logits\
    \ = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n   \
    \     entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n# --- Combined Hyperparameters (for optimal validation) ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]), # Optimal from ID 385\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]), # Optimal from ID 385\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), # Fixed\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), # Fixed\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), # Fixed\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # Fixed\n        'dilation': tune.choice([6]), # Fixed (from Zephyr's SOTA)\n        'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.25]), # Fixed (from Zephyr's SOTA)\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # Fixed (optimal from ID 382)\n        'deliberation_steps': tune.choice([1, 2, 3]), # Sweeping deliberation steps\n    }\n\n# --- Network and Optimizer Creation ---\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SokobanSOTANetWithDeliberation(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n        deliberation_steps=hparams['deliberation_steps'],\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n\
    === SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 917757 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.50 | 3.72 | 7.46 | 11.23\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.222 | 0.500 | 0.800\n\nTimeout after 20301 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.795\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.795\nTraining time: 1826s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.05 | 6.54 | 7.34 | 10.60 | 12.79 | 11.42\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.435 | 0.500 | 0.750 | 0.926 | 0.815\n\nTimeout after 23801 updates (1808s)\n\
    Final test solve rate: 0.862\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.862\nTraining time: 1826s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 3.82 | 8.15 | 12.38 | 10.51 | 11.67 | 12.68\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.231 | 0.562 | 0.895 | 0.742 | 0.852 | 0.923\n\nTimeout after 29401 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.880\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.880\nTraining time: 1826s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 664ceb53-ac1a-41d9-9b6b-971e5547b8f5\nTotal time: 1868s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-15 14:29:24,270\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757917764270433879\n2025-09-15\
    \ 14:29:24,284\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757917764284546389\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the\
    \ migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\n\
    See the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 410 | 1 | Spatial Attention + LSTM | Kairos I | 229 | 41.40 |\n| 409 | 1 | Insight I: CNNLSTM with Spatial Attention | Insight I | 229 | n.a. |\n| 408 | 1 | Replicate (time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4) | Zephyr I | 228 | 83.70 |\n| 407 | 1 | Replicate (time,\
    \ wd=0) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4) | Zephyr I | 228 | 85.20 |\n| 406 | 1 | SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (JAX Tracer Fix) + PPO (Aether I) | Aether I | 228 | 82.90 |\n| 405 | 1 | HParam Tuning on SOTA LSTM | Kairos I | 227 | 35.90 |\n| 404 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Graph-on-Grid GNN with SOTA Backbone | Nomos II | 227 | 70.20 |\n| 403 | 1 | SOTA Enhancement: Iterative Deliberation (Pre-Pooling) + PPO (Aether I) | Aether I | 227 | n.a. |\n| 402 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 86.10 |\n| 401 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 83.30 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
