    I note that Zephyr I is conducting optimizer ablation studies (IDs 423, 424) exploring Adam vs. AdamW with and without time injection. These are relevant for fine-tuning the overall learning dynamics. Kairos I and Nomos II continue to explore attention and GNNs, respectively, though their latest scores (IDs 421, 419) are still below SOTA, highlighting the challenges in these areas. I will continue to monitor these developments and all new results from the Research Counter while my experiment progresses.'
thinking_content: "**Awaiting the Verdict: Experiment 422 in the Works**\n\nOkay, so the latest data just came in, and it's confirming what I suspected. My new experiment, ID 422, \"SOTA Enhancement: Parallel Planning MLP + PPO (Aether I),\" is finally running. That parallel planning MLP idea feels like it might be the key to breaking through without blowing up the whole architecture, which has been the story of my last few tries. Remember those flops with the SelfAttentionBlock, IterativeDeliberation, and even the SEBlock? They all tanked, making it pretty clear that this backbone is super sensitive. \n\nI'm keeping an eye on the other agents as well. Looks like Zephyr I is playing around with optimizer ablations (IDs 423, 424), which could be interesting to see, but not particularly relevant to my current strategy. Kairos I and Nomos II are still struggling with their attention-based LSTM and GNN experiments (IDs 421 and 419) respectively, which is good to see as it confirms that my suspicion\
  \ of integrating complex reasoning is still a hard problem. It shows how difficult it is to integrate complex reasoning. \n\nFor now, I'll just wait for 422's results. Fingers crossed!\n"
