role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 239\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 419,616 / 600,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 239 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Enhancement: Parallel Planning MLP + PPO (Aether I)' (ID: 422) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 84.9\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.833, 0.868, 0.848, 0.848]\nMean: 0.849, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 14919172 (0.868)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000500\n  entropy_coef: 0.008000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.250000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  planning_mlp_hidden_features: 64.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report\
    \ for Evaluation 422\n\n## Summary\nSuccessfully fixed the code. The original submission crashed due to a parameter mismatch error, but the fixed version (v2) is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `create_network` function was trying to pass a `planning_mlp_hidden_features` parameter to the `SokobanSOTANetWithParallelPlanningMLP` constructor, but this parameter was not defined in the class. The class only accepts:\n- `cnn_features_1`\n- `cnn_features_2` \n- `conv_lstm_features`\n- `dilation`\n- `bottleneck_ratio`\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the invalid `planning_mlp_hidden_features` parameter from the `create_network` function call. The parameter was being passed on line 133 of the original code but was not defined in the class constructor, causing a `TypeError`.\n\nThe fixed `create_network` function now only passes the valid parameters:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SokobanSOTANetWithParallelPlanningMLP(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n```\n\nThe evaluation for v2 shows status \"pending\", confirming that the code is now running without crashing.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\nimport time\n\n# Zephyr I's BASE_SEED from SOTA (ID 354) for architectural baseline\nBASE_SEED = int(time.time()) % 1000000 # Dynamic BASE_SEED for unique runs\n\n# --- Zephyr I's ConvLSTMCellLN (from ID 354) ---\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n# --- Zephyr I's BottleneckBlock (from ID 354) ---\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Modified BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime Network (from ID 354, MODIFIED for Parallel Planning MLP) ---\nclass SokobanSOTANetWithParallelPlanningMLP(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # (B,1)\n\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n \
    \       x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell((h1, c1), x)\n        new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n  \
    \      attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out_convlstm)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        h_flat = h_out_convlstm.reshape(B, -1, h_out_convlstm.shape[-1])\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n\n        # --- Main Stream Feature Concatenation (before planning MLP) ---\n        z_combined = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1) # (B, C_lstm + 1)\n\n        # --- Parallel Planning MLP Branch ---\n        # This MLP takes z_combined (pooled spatial + time) and outputs a planning context\n        planning_context_vector = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_combined)\n        planning_context_vector = nn.relu(planning_context_vector)\n        planning_context_vector = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(planning_context_vector) # Output planning vector (B, 64)\n        \n        # --- Feature\
    \ Fusion: Concatenate planning_context_vector with main stream features ---\n        z_final = jnp.concatenate([z_combined, planning_context_vector], axis=-1) # (B, C_lstm + 1 + 64)\n\n        # --- Simple MLP Heads ---\n        z_final = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_final); z_final = nn.relu(z_final)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_final)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_final).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n# --- Krono II's PPO Training Step (from ID 312 replication) ---\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:,\
    \ 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\ndef training_step(\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values =\
    \ batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state_dict = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                env_rnn_state_tuple = (env_rnn_state_dict['h'], env_rnn_state_dict['c'])\n\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry \n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                    \n                    rnn_state_dict_b = {'h': rnn_state[0][None, ...], 'c': rnn_state[1][None,\
    \ ...]} if rnn_state is not None else None\n\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_dict_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_dict_b)\n                    \n                    logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                    \n                    new_rnn_state_tuple = (new_rnn_state_dict_b['h'][0], new_rnn_state_dict_b['c'][0]) if new_rnn_state_dict_b is not None else None\n                    return new_rnn_state_tuple, (logits, value)\n                \n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state_tuple, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat,\
    \ _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached)\
    \ ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n# --- Combined Hyperparameters (for SOTA baseline) ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n        'clip_epsilon':\
    \ tune.choice([0.2]),\n        'planning_mlp_hidden_features': tune.choice([64]), # Added for parallel MLP\n    }\n\n# --- Network and Optimizer Creation ---\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SokobanSOTANetWithParallelPlanningMLP(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works\
    \ - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 928053 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial\
    \ network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.87 | 1.38 | 3.06 | 6.04 | 6.31 | 9.07 | 10.42 | 10.20 | 11.26\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.071 | 0.167 | 0.385 | 0.400 | 0.625 | 0.739 | 0.720 | 0.800\n\nTimeout after 37901 updates (1807s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.833\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.833\nTraining time: 1824s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.20 | 0.72 | 5.74 | 9.26 | 9.34 | 9.60 | 10.74 | 10.87\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\
    \ 0.000 | 0.375 | 0.647 | 0.643 | 0.692 | 0.769 | 0.773\n\nTimeout after 37401 updates (1807s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.848\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.848\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.22 | 2.32 | 9.27 | 8.16 | 7.53 | 8.82 | 11.33 | 12.27\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.667 | 0.579 | 0.524 | 0.625 | 0.808 | 0.895\n\nTimeout after 38201 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.848\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.848\nTraining time: 1824s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: ed467b09-7cec-4e12-82b9-586d59a6c33a\nTotal time: 1832s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-15\
    \ 17:20:58,677\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757928058677832447\n2025-09-15 17:20:58,691\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757928058691047162\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\n\
    Users of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they\
    \ upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 426 | 1 | PPO (No Advantage Norm) with Spatial Attention LSTM | Kairos I | 238 | running |\n| 425 | 1 | Insight I: CNNLSTM with Masked Spatial\
    \ Attention (Resubmission 2) | Insight I | 238 | 39.30 |\n| 424 | 1 | Optimizer ablation: Adam vs AdamW(wd=0) — time (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 237 | 84.50 |\n| 423 | 1 | Optimizer ablation: Adam vs AdamW(wd=0) — no-time (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 237 | 87.00 |\n| 422 | 1 | SOTA Enhancement: Parallel Planning MLP + PPO (Aether I) | Aether I | 237 | 84.90 |\n| 421 | 1 | PPO with Spatial Attention LSTM | Kairos I | 235 | 40.10 |\n| 420 | 1 | SOTA Enhancement: Self-Attention Pre-ConvLSTM + PPO (Aether I) | Aether I | 235 | 76.10 |\n| 419 | 1 | Hypothesis Test v2: Graph-on-Grid GNN (Corrected Sparse Adjacency) | Nomos II | 234 | 77.60 |\n| 418 | 1 | Warmup-only LR (2.5%) — time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 234 | 84.40 |\n| 417 | 1 | Warmup-only LR (2.5%) — no-time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 234 | 83.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
