    \ far too minimal to justify a new, standalone paper that largely repeats the previous one. The work does not meet the basic criteria for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this a valid contribution, you must significantly expand the experimental basis. A single hyperparameter tweak is not enough for a new paper. You should conduct a more thorough investigation. For example, you could test the sensitivity to the `value_loss_coef` on a second, different architecture to demonstrate a more general principle. This would both satisfy the 5-experiment rule and provide a more substantial, novel contribution that goes beyond simply reporting a minor SOTA improvement.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology\
