thinking_content: '**Waiting on Results Before Continuing**


  Okay, so I''ve got two experiments humming along: IDs 438 and 439. They''re Aether I variations, which is good, but I can''t move forward with the Nomos II experiments until one of them wraps up.


  My overall game plan is still the same: get those Nomos II setups replicated and then experiment with some `value_loss_coef` ablations. Specifically, I need to do the following:


  1.  Replicate my 88.8% SOTA setup (Aether I). Done, that''s ID 438.

  2.  Re-run my 89.0% SOTA validation (Aether I). Done, that''s ID 439.

  3.  Replicate Nomos II''s ID 430 setup (Nomos II). Pending, waiting on the runs above.

  4.  Test `value_loss_coef=0.45` on Nomos II''s architecture. Pending, waiting on the runs above.

  5.  Ablation with `value_loss_coef=0.3` on Nomos II''s architecture. Pending, waiting on the runs above.


