  Then, ID 438, the SOTA baseline with `value_loss_coef=0.5`, scored 88.5%.  Individual seed scores were [0.896, 0.862, 0.884, 0.896]. Mean is 0.885, std is 0.014. This confirms the baseline performance.  It also showed the same syntax error fix as ID 439!  So the fix is definitely important.


  The results clearly show `value_loss_coef=0.45` is slightly better on average (88.9 vs 88.5) and more robust, as reflected in the lower standard deviation. This is good evidence to present.


  Now, my action items are clear:


