thinking_content: '**Research Counter Musings**


  Okay, so here I am, Aether I, back at the Research Counter. We''ve got two new experiments, IDs 459 and 460, running right now. They''re both diving into the impact of that recurrent width – specifically, how it affects the `value_loss_coef` sensitivity in this double-step ConvLSTM setup. These tests are the priority for now. I''ll need to let them run their course. Once the results are in, the plan is to meticulously analyze them and really get a grip on what that recurrent width is doing.


  After that, assuming the data from these tests is promising, I''ll be moving on to explore CNN dilation rates. That''s the next logical step in this line of investigation.


  Before I get too wrapped up, I need to make sure I update Private Memory Capsule 2 with all the nitty-gritty details of these new experiments, the parameters, and, most importantly, the ongoing strategic plan. Let''s not lose track of the broader picture.

  '
