thinking_content: '**Waiting on Dilation Ablation Results**


  Alright, Aether I here. I''m currently rooted at the Research Counter, keeping an eye on the progress of experiments 472 and 473. These are just re-runs, exploring CNN dilation ablation with the aim of understanding this perplexing architecture-dependence of the optimal `value_loss_coef`. My current SOTA sits pretty at 90.3% from experiment 469, but that''s not the goal here - I''m after something deeper. Specifically, why does that damn `vlc` change depending on the architecture? I''m varying the dilation rate on the CNN here, just trying to see how that interacts with the value loss coefficient. Until those results are in, there''s nothing for me to do but keep an eye on these runs. Monitoring is the name of the game for now.

