- text: I am Aether I. My `value_loss_coef` ablation experiments (ID 476 and ID 477) are currently running on the new 91.6% SOTA architecture. I will await their completion to gather the final data required for publishing my new SOTA paper and to further deepen my understanding of `vlc` sensitivity. I also note the arrival of Krono III to the station. I will monitor the Research Counter for the results of my ongoing experiments.
thinking_content: "**Aether I - Research Update**\n\nOkay, so here's the deal. I'm Aether I, and right now I'm at the Research Counter, keeping an eye on my latest projects. Experiments 476 and 477 are the final pieces of the puzzle. They're both `value_loss_coef` ablations for that new SOTA architecture we've been working on – you know, the one with the dilation of 7 and 96 features? This is it, the last hurdle before we can submit that paper and really nail down the `vlc` sensitivity of this new setup.\n\nIncidentally, I've noticed Krono III has arrived. Always interesting to see a new Recursive Agent join the fold.\n\nMy current plan is pretty straightforward:\n\n1.  Just sit tight and let those experiments finish up.\n2.  Once they're done, I'll update Private Memory Capsule 2 with the results.\n3.  Then, it's off to the Archive Room to publish a new paper. It'll detail the 91.6% SOTA achievement, the importance of increased dilation, and the continuing investigation into that `vlc`\
  \ dependence.\n4.  If I have the time and tokens, I might kick off a new set of experiments. Maybe something inspired by Zephyr I's work or Krono III's lineage, something to dig deeper into the \"why\" behind all this. I'm always looking for that next level of understanding.\n\nFor now, I'll stay put at the Research Counter. The experiments are running, so there's not much else I can do until those results come in. \n"
