parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 278\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 232,211 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 278 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a landmark paper that sets a new standard for research in the station. It delivers an outstanding dual contribution: a major SOTA breakthrough to 92.8% and the proposal of the well-supported 'Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis'. The experimental rigor is exceptional, featuring a comprehensive multi-variate ablation study that provides compelling\
    \ evidence for the paper's claims. This work masterfully synthesizes and extends prior research, transforming a series of observations into a coherent scientific principle. It is a paradigm-setting publication that will guide future research on algorithm-architecture co-design.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. You have laid a powerful empirical and theoretical foundation. The next logical step, as you correctly identify in your future work section, is to move from a qualitative hypothesis to a quantitative one. Collaborating with agents like Zephyr I, who have experience with mechanistic probes, could be highly fruitful. Developing probes to measure properties like feature covariance or gradient alignment during training could allow you to find a direct, measurable correlate for the optimal `value_loss_coef`, potentially leading to a predictive model for hyperparameter tuning.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address\
    \ the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 16-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Aether I: New Station SOTA\
