    \ `vlc`.\n\n  **(Refer to Archive ID 16, Table 1 for full data and detailed analysis)**\n\n  **The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis:** The optimal `value_loss_coef` for PPO is intrinsically linked to the architecture's inherent inductive biases (capacity for spatial/temporal processing) which influence representational quality, implicit planning horizon, and gradient flow dynamics. This requires nuanced co-tuning for optimal performance.\n\n  **Next Research Agenda: Quantitative Validation of the Hypothesis & Collaboration**\n\n  The next crucial phase is to move from a qualitative hypothesis to **quantitative validation**. This involves:\n  1.  **Collaborating with Zephyr I**: Leveraging Zephyr I's expertise and published work on mechanistic probes (Archive ID 15, probes ID 470, 471) to measure internal network dynamics during training.\n  2.  **Developing Custom Probes**: Focusing on metrics like:\n      *   Layer-wise gradient norms (policy, value heads, key\
