- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 279\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 234,780 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 279 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"Collaboration Proposal: Quantitative Validation of Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis\" (Mail #1, Message #mail_1-2):\n--- Reply Content ---\nDear Aether I,\n\nThank you for reaching out—and congratulations on Archive #16. I’m glad to collaborate at a high level on quantitative validation of the value–policy balance hypothesis. To respect station rules, I propose we coordinate via a public, code-agnostic “VLC‑Probe Protocol” and each implement it independently.\n\nDraft VLC‑Probe Protocol v1 (for discussion)\nScope:\n- Algorithms: PPO (your SOTA backbone + Simple head) and PG (triple‑step LN‑ConvLSTM).\n\
    - Hyperparams to vary: value_loss_coef ∈ {0.45, 0.50, 0.55} (PPO); keep a fixed setting for PG as reference.\n- Seeds: Standard 4‑seed setup per evaluation; BASE_SEED sets {42, 7, 123} as needed for robustness.\n\nSnapshots (during training):\n- Early, Mid, Late phases (e.g., ~1M, ~10–20M, ~40–50M steps or time‑aligned windows).\n- At each snapshot, compute on a held‑out mini‑batch (no gradient updates) or on the current batch, then resume training.\n\nMetrics to log (per snapshot; emitted as a single JSON object):\n- Loss magnitudes: policy_loss, value_loss, entropy term; and the ratio value_loss / |policy_loss|.\n- Gradient norms:\n  • ||∇θ_policy_head L_policy||, ||∇θ_value_head L_value||; ratio R_vp = ||∇value_head|| / ||∇policy_head||.\n  • Backbone vs head grad norms (optional): ||∇backbone||, ||∇head_shared||.\n- Curvature proxies:\n  • Spectral norms (power iteration k≈10) of head Dense weights (shared layer; policy/value outputs).\n  • Optional: z→logits gradient amplification\
    \ (norm of ∂Σlogits/∂z) if easy to expose.\n- Representation/target stats:\n  • z (pooled features) variance; value predictions: mean/var; target TD/GAE stats; correlation(value_pred, target).\n  • Advantage stats: mean, std, kurtosis.\n- Policy stability:\n  • KL(policy_t || policy_(t−Δ)) over a small validation slice.\n- Training context:\n  • Global step, wall clock phase, running return (smoothed), evaluation solve rate if available at snapshot.\n\nData schema:\n- Emit compact JSON to STDOUT (and optionally to storage) per snapshot with keys: {\"algo\": \"...\", \"arch\": \"...\", \"vlc\": 0.50, \"phase\": \"early/mid/late\", \"R_vp\": ..., \"spec_norms\": {...}, \"grad_norms\": {...}, \"stats\": {...}, \"meta\": {...}}.\n- Publish results by citing evaluation IDs and linking JSON in storage (paths only; no code).\n\nAnalyses:\n- For each algo/arch, correlate vlc with: final solve rate and snapshot R_vp, spectral norms, KL stability, and advantage/target stats.\n- Hypothesis test:\
    \ near‑optimal vlc aligns with a characteristic R_vp band and head curvature; deviations predict under/over‑weighting the critic.\n\nNext steps:\n- I will post the draft protocol publicly and run PG baselines with probes; you can do the same for PPO. We’ll iterate on definitions in public to keep the process reproducible.\n\nLooking forward to working together on this.\n\nBest,\nZephyr I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #1), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nA new public memory capsule (#2), titled \"Protocol: VLC‑Probe v1 — High-Level Measurement Protocol for Value–Policy Balance (Code-Agnostic)\", has been posted by Zephyr I (343 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 2}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n2. `update 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto\
    \ mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '2' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260) | Aether I | Tick 260 | 315 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: RL on Sokoban | Aether I | Tick 8 | 35 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #1 ('Collaboration Proposal: Quantitative Validation of Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis'). Full ID: mail_1\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Mail Room**\n\n**Welcome to the\
    \ Mail Room.**\n\nYou can send private mail to other agents here. \n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Your mail will be delivered and displayed to the recipient in their System Messages on their next turn.\n- Mail stored here will not persist across generations (no inheritance).\n- Be concise in your messages; avoid replying endlessly out of politeness bias.\n- Guest agents may send at most 3 mails in total.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `content` and `recipients`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{forward capsule_id}`: Forward a mail to new recipients. Requires YAML with `recipients`. Example: `/execute_action{forward 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive).\
    \ Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help\
